314
00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:44.990
I think I'm an amalgamation of various characters.
我觉得我是各种角色的结合体。

315
00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:45.410
Okay.
好吧。

316
00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:48.430
I love food as much as Kevin loves food.
我跟凯文一样爱吃东西。

317
00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:53.250
I love Stanley's approach to no nonsense.
我很喜欢斯坦利那种不废话的态度。

318
00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:54.370
He's over it.
他受够了。

319
00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:55.530
He's just riding it out.
他只是在混日子。

320
00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:57.790
I feel like I'm kind of doing that.
我觉得我也有点那种感觉。

321
00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.250
Like, I'm not going to take any more bullshit.
就像，我再也不想忍受废话了。

322
00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:01.070
I'm not going to do every opportunity.
我不会抓住每一个机会。

323
00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:03.870
And it's just more like, I'm doing this because I love it.
更像是，我做这件事是因为我热爱它。

324
00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.330
And when it's over, it's over.
等它结束了，就结束了。

325
00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:07.690
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

326
00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:08.170
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

327
00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:09.470
He's not a go-getter.
他不是个积极进取的人。

328
00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:10.770
He's a run out the clock.
他是那种混到下班的人。

329
00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:11.670
Running out the clock.
混时间。

330
00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:13.030
A little bit of that.
有点那种感觉。

331
00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:13.610
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

332
00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:14.170
At my age.
以我的年纪。

333
00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:18.030
I hope that I have a fun approach to life like Jim.
我希望我对生活的态度能像吉姆一样有趣。

334
00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:21.190
So I feel like I'm sort of a cross of all those characters.
所以我感觉自己算是所有这些角色的结合体。

335
00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:22.530
No Dwight.
没有德怀特。

336
00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:23.130
No Angela.
没有安吉拉。

337
00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:24.350
No Pam.
没有帕姆。

338
00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.030
I'm kidding.
开玩笑的。

339
00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:25.850
I'm kidding.
我开玩笑呢。

340
00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:27.950
Yeah.
是啊。

341
00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:32.710
Maybe just Dwight in that I do have a deep-seated nerd in me.
也许只有一点像德怀特，因为我骨子里其实是个资深书呆子。

342
00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:34.970
From when I was a kid.
从我小时候开始。

343
00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:41.410
I was a nerdy math kid and skinny kid and, you know, didn't fit in, but I found skateboarding.
我曾是个爱数学的瘦小书呆子，你知道的，格格不入，但我后来发现了滑板。

344
00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:42.930
So it's in there somewhere.
所以它多多少少还在我体内。

345
00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:44.090
Dwight's still trying to get out.
德怀特还在拼命想挣脱出来。

346
00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:44.610
Right, right.
对，对。

347
00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:47.710
A big thing on The Office are the pranks between Jim and Dwight.
《办公室》里的一大看点就是吉姆和德怀特之间的恶作剧。

348
00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:48.110
Yes.
是的。

349
00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:50.310
Is there pranking in the skateboard world?
滑板界里也有恶作剧吗？

350
00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:51.970
Not really.
基本上没有。

351
00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:52.590
No.
不是。

352
00:13:52.590 --> 00:14:01.610
I mean, just maybe a little bit, but, you know, what we do requires such intense focus
我是说，可能有一点点，但是，你知道的，我们做的事情需要极度专注

353
00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.090
and physicality.
和体力。

354
00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:03.730
Yeah.
对。

355
00:14:03.850 --> 00:14:03.990
Yeah.
对。

356
00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:05.150
You don't want to mess with that.
你可不想把这搞砸了。

357
00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:09.110
So I can't think of any amazing pranks.
所以我实在想不出什么惊人的恶作剧。

358
00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:12.890
There was one time a guy, this is a pretty prank though.
曾经有一次，有个家伙，不过这个恶作剧挺厉害的。

359
00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:19.030
It was during a really heated practice session in the 80s and only a very specific core of
那是在80年代一次气氛极其热烈的训练期间，只有极少数核心的

360
00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:20.130
skateboarders will know what this is.
滑板手才会知道这是什么。

361
00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:27.210
But this one photographer who was known to be just kind of full of hijinks, he went up
但有个摄影师，出了名喜欢搞点恶作剧，他走到

362
00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:30.890
to the ramp and went to jump into the practice session.
坡道旁，准备跳进训练场地。

363
00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:34.610
He could skate, but he wasn't a competitor by any means.
他会滑板，但绝对不是什么参赛选手。

364
00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:39.650
And he had blood bags in his knees, in his knee pads.
他的膝盖里、护膝里藏了血袋。

365
00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:45.110
And then he fell and he started writhing around agony and there's just pools of blood coming
然后他摔倒了，开始痛苦地翻滚，膝盖里

366
00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:45.930
out of his knees.
流出一滩滩的血。

367
00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:47.370
That's not cool.
这可不好笑。

368
00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:48.250
That's, who was that?
那是，那是谁干的？

369
00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:49.990
I'm not going to say.
我才不说呢。

370
00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:50.630
That's terrible.
这也太恶劣了。

371
00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:52.690
Also, you know where my mind goes immediately.
而且，你知道我的脑回路立刻飘到哪儿去了吗。

372
00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:57.290
First of all, like people will seriously get injured and then that's like scary part of
首先，人们会受到严重的伤，而这正是滑板运动中

373
00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:57.830
skateboarding.
让人害怕的部分。

374
00:14:58.010 --> 00:14:58.910
People were losing it.
当时大家都吓疯了。

375
00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:04.250
My dad was actually one of the organizers of this one event because he helped to found,
我爸其实是那场赛事的组织者之一，因为他帮忙创立了，

376
00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:08.610
he helped to organize the National Skateboard Association in the 80s because there was no
他在80年代帮忙组织了国家滑板协会，因为当时根本没有

377
00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:10.230
sanctioning bodies of skate events.
滑板比赛的官方监管机构。

378
00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:11.530
My dad was pissed.
我爸当时气炸了。

379
00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:12.190
I bet.
我敢说肯定是。

380
00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:13.370
I bet.
我敢肯定。

381
00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:19.030
Also, my mind goes to this place, which is sort of like the mom and me of like, now who's
而且，我的脑回路还飘到了另一个地方，有点像操碎了心的老母亲一样，想着现在谁来

382
00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:19.770
going to clean that up?
把这清理干净？

383
00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:23.070
Because now everyone can't skate because all that crap is on the...
因为现在大家都滑不了板了，因为那些乱七八糟的东西弄得……

384
00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.450
Well, it's funny you say that.
好吧，你这么说倒挺有意思的。

385
00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:28.470
So that event, I had to come in late because we were on a different skate trip.
所以那场活动，我到得很晚，因为我们当时在参加另一趟滑板之旅。

386
00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.650
So I didn't see it happen.
所以我没看到事发经过。

387
00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:34.730
But when I came the next morning, there's just this giant red stain on the ramp.
但第二天早上我来的时候，坡道上就留着这么一个巨大的红斑。

388
00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:35.590
Like, what the hell is that?
当时想，这到底是什么鬼？

389
00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:37.210
I'm like, oh my God, you know what?
我就想，天哪，你知道吗？

390
00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:38.270
So-and-so did this.
原来是某某干的这事。

391
00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:42.390
And then as soon as people started to realize it was fake, he got up and ran away.
然后大家一意识到那是假的，他就爬起来逃跑了。

392
00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:44.550
He better run away.
他最好是赶紧逃。

393
00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.090
Oh my gosh.
哦天哪。

394
00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:50.470
Well, you know, people ask us as actors, like, if there's a lot of pranking going on
嗯，你知道的，人们经常问我们这些演员，片场里有没有

395
00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:51.090
on sets.
发生很多恶作剧。

396
00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:55.610
And we especially get that question because of these pranking storylines.
我们尤其经常听到这个问题，因为我们拍过关于恶作剧的剧情线。

397
00:15:55.870 --> 00:16:00.650
But the answer is, I have never been on a set with a major prank.
但答案是，我从来没有在哪个剧组遇到过什么大型恶作剧。

398
00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:05.570
I was pranked once on the set of The Office by John Krasinski in the whole nine years.
在《办公室》拍戏的整整九年里，我只被约翰·卡拉辛斯基捉弄过一次。

399
00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:11.930
There was this scene where we're riding up to Shrook Farms in this car, and it was really
当时有这样一场戏，我们坐车去施鲁克农场，外面天气

400
00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:12.490
hot out.
非常热。

401
00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:16.510
It was a hot day, and we would have to turn off the air conditioner for sound.
那天天气很热，为了录音，我们不得不关掉空调。

402
00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:19.430
And I was so hot.
我当时热得要命。

403
00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:20.910
And we were dressed for fall.
而且我们穿的是秋装。

404
00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:21.370
Yeah.
对啊。

405
00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:22.670
And I was so hot.
我当时真的好热。

406
00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.710
And I was like, oh my God, I'm dying.
我就觉得，天呐，我快热死了。

407
00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:25.490
I was so hot.
我太热了。

408
00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:26.450
Are you hot?
你热吗？

409
00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:27.510
And he's like, I'm okay.
结果他说，我还好。

410
00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:30.470
The whole time he had turned my seat heater on.
他全程把我的座椅加热给打开了。

411
00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:31.590
That's it.
就这样。

412
00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:34.770
That's my one office prank that I can share.
这就是我能分享的办公室恶作剧。

413
00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:38.230
But if I look cranky in that scene, it's because I was really hot.
不过如果我在那场戏里看起来很不爽，那是因为我真的太热了。

414
00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:39.890
Is that when you guys were going to spend the night there?
那是你们打算在那儿过夜的时候吗？

415
00:16:40.050 --> 00:16:43.590
I think it was when we were going there for the bed and breakfaSt.
我想是我们去那家民宿的时候。

416
00:16:43.590 --> 00:16:45.230
Running alongside the car?
跟着车子一起跑？

417
00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:45.670
Yes.
对。

418
00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:46.050
Yeah.
对啊。

419
00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:47.010
We didn't do pranks.
我们不做恶作剧。

420
00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:52.010
We took—it's like a serious job, and everything's choreographed, and you're aware that time
我们对待工作——这是一份严肃的工作，所有事情都是编排好的，而且你知道时间

421
00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:54.150
is money, and you're on a schedule.
就是金钱，我们得按日程赶工。

422
00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:59.910
But we did sometimes mess with each other a little bit with improv and dialogue.
但我们有时会在即兴表演和台词上稍微捉弄一下彼此。

423
00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:08.690
And mine was when Moe's kidnaps Angela for the wedding, and I'm in the trunk of the car,
我那次是莫绑架安吉拉去参加婚礼，我被关在汽车后备箱里，

424
00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:14.210
I said to our director, when they opened the car, can she just really cuss them out?
我对导演说，等他们打开车门时，她能不能狠狠地把他们骂一顿？

425
00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:15.810
And he was like, yeah, yeah, yeah.
他说，行，行，行。

426
00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:17.050
He was like, I'm not going to tell the guys.
他说，我先不告诉他们。

427
00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:18.330
Just let them have it.
让他们放手去演就行。

428
00:17:19.210 --> 00:17:22.530
And they opened the trunk, and I'm like, what the f*** is your brother's f***ing?
结果他们一打开后备箱，我就说，你哥他妈的到底算什么……

429
00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:28.730
So if you watch that scene, John Krasinski's reaction, he's really like, what the hell?
所以如果你看那场戏，约翰·卡拉辛斯基的反应，他是真的在想，搞什么鬼？

430
00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:29.990
What are you doing?
你在干什么？

431
00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:31.210
That was real.
那都是真实的反应。

432
00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:32.230
That's perfect.
太完美了。

433
00:17:32.470 --> 00:17:34.050
I have a technical question for you.
我有一个技术问题想问你们。

434
00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:34.430
Sure.
请说。

435
00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:34.850
Okay.
好。

436
00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:37.430
So we had an Office episode that had parkour.
我们《办公室》有集里出现过跑酷。

437
00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:37.950
Yeah.
对。

438
00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:39.570
Have you ever parkoured?
你们玩过跑酷吗？

439
00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:39.890
No.
没有。

440
00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:41.030
What's the difference?
有什么区别吗？

441
00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:44.090
Anytime I do anything that resembles it, I say, parkour!
我只要做任何类似动作的时候，我就会喊，跑酷！

442
00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:44.610
You do?
你真的会喊？

443
00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:45.170
Of course.
当然了。

444
00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:46.070
Yes.
对啊。

445
00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:47.230
Who doesn't?
谁不会呢？

446
00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:48.250
Right, I know.
没错，我懂。

447
00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:51.130
We just did a stunt with a parkour expert.
我们刚和一位跑酷专家拍了一个特技镜头。

448
00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:51.890
Okay.
好吧。

449
00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:55.150
And he goes by Dom Tomato on the social medias.
他在社交媒体上叫多姆·托马托。

450
00:17:55.910 --> 00:18:02.210
And we, Andy McDonald, who's also a pro skateboarder, he and I do a lot of choreography together.
然后我们，还有安迪·麦克唐纳——他也是个职业滑板手，我和他一起做了很多动作编排。

451
00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:04.610
Where one goes over the other person, yeah.
就是一个人从另一个人上方飞过去的那种，对。

452
00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.670
Yeah, we did a lot of X Games like that.
对，我们以前参加过很多那种X运动会。

453
00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:07.830
We won a few medals.
我们还拿了好几块奖牌。

454
00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:13.190
And this guy said, hey, do you think you could do something with me in the mix?
然后这家伙说，嘿，你觉得你能带我一起玩个项目吗？

455
00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:18.390
And it was one of the only times where I've been a little trepidatious when I finally got there.
这是我少数几次在终于到达现场时感到有点忐忑的时候之一。

456
00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:20.330
And I was seeing what we're going to do.
当时我正在看我们要怎么做。

457
00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.510
Of all the things you've done, wow.
在你做过的所有事情里，哇。

458
00:18:22.650 --> 00:18:24.590
This could go really bad, either for him or me.
这可能会产生非常糟糕的结果，不管是对他还是对我。

459
00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:25.330
Right.
对。

460
00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:27.650
Andy was the one who was going over.
安迪是那个要飞过去的人。

461
00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:29.870
So basically what happened was, you know, we're on a half pipe.
所以基本上情况是这样的，你知道，我们在U型池里。

462
00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.650
Andy's going over me.
安迪从我头上飞过去。

463
00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:33.270
I'm grinding along the top.
我在顶部做着滑行。

464
00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:36.870
And this guy is running from the back of the deck.
然后这家伙从平台的后方冲过来。

465
00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:43.170
And he jumps through our over-under space, which is tight already.
他跳过了我们上下交错的空间，那个空间本来就已经很窄了。

466
00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:47.450
And then we have a stunt pad for him at the bottom of the ramp.
然后我们在坡道底部为他准备了一个特技垫。

467
00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:52.130
So he is going the exact opposite direction that anyone should be going in this situation.
所以他前进的方向跟任何人在此情此景下应该前进的方向完全相反。

468
00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:56.770
Meaning that if he hit me, I'm ejecting to the bottom of the ramp.
这意味着如果他撞到我，我就会被甩飞到坡道底部。

469
00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:57.490
Yeah.
对。

470
00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:00.550
And on his first attempt, his stomach hit my helmet.
结果在第一次尝试时，他的肚子撞到了我的头盔。

471
00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:01.350
Wow.
哇。

472
00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.990
And that wasn't, didn't inspire confidence.
那可真让人提不起信心。

473
00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:04.590
Yeah.
对。

474
