00:30:01.610 --> 00:30:04.710
probably the least qualified to ask you these questions.
大概是最没资格问你这些问题的人了。

846
00:30:04.990 --> 00:30:09.010
Yes, and I know these are questions that you've probably answered many times, but I think
是的，而且我知道这些问题你可能已经回答过很多次了，但我认为

847
00:30:09.010 --> 00:30:13.490
that for our listeners, this might be, like, very new, so we're excited.
对我们的听众来说，这可能非常新鲜，所以我们很兴奋。

848
00:30:13.630 --> 00:30:13.950
Thank you.
谢谢。

849
00:30:14.210 --> 00:30:14.470
Sure.
不客气。

850
00:30:14.470 --> 00:30:18.630
So, everyone knows you for doing the first 900.
所以，大家都知道你是第一个完成900度旋转的人。

851
00:30:19.370 --> 00:30:24.490
This is a trick that took you, like, seven years to master, or more?
这是你花了好大劲，比如七年甚至更久才学会的绝招吗？

852
00:30:24.650 --> 00:30:25.150
More, yeah.
不止，是的。

853
00:30:25.370 --> 00:30:26.070
Yes, but—
是的，但是——

854
00:30:26.070 --> 00:30:29.510
But you've also invented over 100 tricks in your career.
但你在职业生涯中也发明了100多个招式。

855
00:30:29.610 --> 00:30:34.070
Do you have a personal favorite that you've ever done or invented?
你有没有哪个做过或发明过的招式是自己最喜欢的？

856
00:30:35.510 --> 00:30:41.590
Yeah, you know, I learned how to do an Ollie 540, which is basically a one-and-a-half
有啊，你知道的，我学会了奥利540（Ollie 540），这基本上就是在空中转体

857
00:30:41.590 --> 00:30:43.330
spin in the air without grabbing the board.
一圈半，而且双手不抓滑板。

858
00:30:43.750 --> 00:30:44.310
Yeah.
对。

859
00:30:44.310 --> 00:30:49.410
Around 1989, and I tried that trick as a joke.
大约在1989年，我当时只是开玩笑地尝试了这个招式。

860
00:30:49.870 --> 00:30:55.590
I literally did it, was like, ha-ha, crazy, no-handed, and then at some point figured out
我真的做出来了，当时觉得，哈哈，太疯狂了，不抓板，然后不知在什么时候我摸索出

861
00:30:55.590 --> 00:31:00.550
how to sort of scoop the board using my feet and keep it on during the rotation, and I
了如何用双脚去“兜”住滑板，并在旋转过程中让它贴着脚，所以

862
00:31:00.550 --> 00:31:04.750
think that's probably the one that I'm most proud of because I felt like it unlocks a
我觉得这可能是我最自豪的招式，因为我觉得它开启了

863
00:31:04.750 --> 00:31:09.550
new direction and a new way to keep your board on your feet.
一个全新的方向，也是一种让滑板紧贴双脚的新方法。

864
00:31:09.730 --> 00:31:10.170
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

865
00:31:10.450 --> 00:31:11.470
Personally, so—
就我个人而言，所以——

866
00:31:11.470 --> 00:31:13.110
It also looks like magic when you do it.
而且你做的时候看起来就像魔法一样。

867
00:31:13.110 --> 00:31:15.290
It just—I was like, how is it there?
简直——我当时就在想，板怎么会一直贴在那儿？

868
00:31:15.410 --> 00:31:20.130
The wild part is that there is a whole new generation of skating, of skaters that have
最疯狂的是，现在有一代全新的滑板运动、新一代的滑手

869
00:31:20.130 --> 00:31:21.910
figured out how to take that to new heights.
他们已经琢磨出如何把这个招式带到新的高度。

870
00:31:22.510 --> 00:31:28.850
And there are literally skaters doing Ollie 540s, like, seven or eight feet above the ramp.
真的有滑手能做出奥利540，比如在离滑道七八英尺的高空。

871
00:31:29.050 --> 00:31:32.430
I did it right at the top of the ramp because I couldn't figure out how to keep my board
我当年只能在滑道的最顶端做，因为我想不出怎么能让滑板

872
00:31:32.430 --> 00:31:38.210
on my feet any longer, and they've just unlocked this whole new technique that I love that I
在脚上呆得更久，而他们刚刚解锁了这门全新的技术，我非常喜欢，也很高兴能见证这一切。

873
00:31:38.210 --> 00:31:38.890
get to witness it.
见证这一切。

874
00:31:39.050 --> 00:31:45.250
When you were doing the 900 trick, was there a moment—because you did it—you did so many
当你做900度转体这个动作时，有没有那么一个瞬间——因为你做过——你尝试了那么多

875
00:31:45.250 --> 00:31:45.710
attempts.
次。

876
00:31:46.270 --> 00:31:47.130
Was there a moment—
有没有那么一个瞬间——

877
00:31:47.130 --> 00:31:49.110
Well, many, many, many before that, yes.
噢，在那之前有过很多很多次，是的。

878
00:31:49.110 --> 00:31:49.750
Many, many, yeah.
很多很多次，对。

879
00:31:49.970 --> 00:31:52.950
Was there a moment where you saw it?
有没有那么一个瞬间，你看到了希望？

880
00:31:53.290 --> 00:31:57.290
Like, was there a moment where it just clicked for you that it made it that one time different
比如说，有没有那么一瞬间，你突然开窍了，觉得这一次和

881
00:31:57.290 --> 00:31:58.590
than all the other times?
以前所有尝试都不一样？

882
00:31:58.810 --> 00:32:03.650
There was, but that happened years prior to when I—when I actually—
有的，但那发生在我——我真正成功——的几年前。

883
00:32:03.650 --> 00:32:04.170
To the X Games.
到世界极限运动会（X Games）为止。

884
00:32:04.250 --> 00:32:04.470
—figured it out.
——琢磨出来的前几年。

885
00:32:04.630 --> 00:32:04.790
Yeah.
对。

886
00:32:05.310 --> 00:32:09.830
There was a moment where I thought, if I really just commit to this, it should work.
曾经有那么一瞬间，我想，如果我真的豁出去全力以赴，这应该能成功。

887
00:32:10.390 --> 00:32:14.670
And it was around 1994, maybe 95.
那大约是在1994年，或者95年吧。

888
00:32:15.790 --> 00:32:17.790
And I committed to a landing.
然后我下定决心要稳稳落地。

889
00:32:18.330 --> 00:32:21.550
To be honest, the reason that I was committing to the landing is because I was running out
说实话，我之所以下定决心要落地，是因为我

890
00:32:21.550 --> 00:32:23.730
of time to skate because I had to go pick up my son at preschool.
滑板的时间快不够了，我得去幼儿园接我儿子。

891
00:32:23.850 --> 00:32:24.530
This is not a joke.
这不是开玩笑。

892
00:32:25.110 --> 00:32:28.470
Like, you know, my son was going to be the last kid at preschool waiting.
你看，我儿子快成幼儿园里最后一个等家长的小朋友了。

893
00:32:28.710 --> 00:32:29.870
So you had to figure it out.
所以你必须得搞定它。

894
00:32:29.990 --> 00:32:33.990
So I got to, like, try to make this stupid trick so I can get out of here and get there
所以我得赶紧试着把这个蠢招式做出来，这样我才能离开这里，按时

895
00:32:33.990 --> 00:32:34.390
on time.
赶到那儿。

896
00:32:35.170 --> 00:32:37.110
And so I just said, okay, this is it.
所以我当时就说，好吧，就是这样了。

897
00:32:37.170 --> 00:32:37.790
I'm committing to it.
我拼了。

898
00:32:37.790 --> 00:32:41.490
And when I went to commit to it, I was leaning too far forward on the landing.
当我准备豁出去落地时，落地时身体前倾得太厉害了。

899
00:32:41.850 --> 00:32:44.370
And I crashed into the bottom of the ramp and broke my rib.
结果我直接撞到了滑道底部，摔断了肋骨。

900
00:32:44.950 --> 00:32:48.190
Still managed to get my son, you know, with a broken rib.
顶着断了的肋骨，我最后还是设法把我儿子接回来了。

901
00:32:48.410 --> 00:32:48.590
Yeah.
是啊。

902
00:32:49.450 --> 00:32:51.630
I mean, this is mid-90s skateboarding.
我是说，这可是90年代中期的滑板运动。

903
00:32:51.750 --> 00:32:54.690
We didn't have a lot of resources or support.
我们没有多少资源或支持。

904
00:32:55.150 --> 00:32:56.850
And I was just doing this because I loved it.
我做这个纯粹是因为我热爱。

905
00:32:57.050 --> 00:32:58.890
You know, ESPN was not going to—
你知道的，ESPN可不会——

906
00:32:58.890 --> 00:32:59.770
Show up there.
出现在那里。

907
00:32:59.910 --> 00:33:01.550
Show up there and be like, hey, you did 900.
出现在那儿然后说，嘿，你完成了900度旋转。

908
00:33:01.690 --> 00:33:02.750
They didn't even know what a 900 was.
他们甚至不知道什么是900度旋转。

909
00:33:03.010 --> 00:33:07.050
You know, this was sort of the dark days of skateboarding, especially of ramp skating.
你知道，这可以说是滑板运动的黑暗时期，尤其是U池滑板。

910
00:33:07.810 --> 00:33:13.370
So long story short, in that moment, I thought, maybe it doesn't work because I had all the
所以长话短说，在那一刻，我想，也许行不通，因为我已经集齐了所有

911
00:33:13.370 --> 00:33:14.150
pieces to the puzzle.
拼图的碎片。

912
00:33:14.390 --> 00:33:14.650
Yeah.
对。

913
00:33:14.810 --> 00:33:19.330
I envisioned making it and I fell forward and, you know, got hurt.
我设想过成功落地，但我向前摔倒了，而且，你知道的，受伤了。

914
00:33:19.530 --> 00:33:22.150
So picked up my son, healed up, whatever.
所以抱起我儿子，养好伤，诸如此类。

915
00:33:22.430 --> 00:33:23.830
And then I kind of put it on the shelf.
然后我基本上把它搁置了。

916
00:33:24.110 --> 00:33:28.130
Tried it off and on every once in a while, but I could never get my—I could never commit
偶尔断断续续地尝试过，但我再也无法像那天那样——我再也无法全身心

917
00:33:28.130 --> 00:33:32.890
to it again in the way that I did that one day because I didn't want to break my rib again.
投入进去了，因为我不想再次摔断肋骨。

918
00:33:32.890 --> 00:33:33.090
Yeah.
对。

919
00:33:33.430 --> 00:33:36.390
Or my collar—I thought my collarbone was broken because it was so high up.
或者锁骨——我以为我的锁骨断了，因为它肿得那么高。

920
00:33:37.150 --> 00:33:37.930
Luckily, it was just a rib.
幸好，只是断了根肋骨。

921
00:33:38.030 --> 00:33:43.090
But so when I was at the X Games and I was starting to get close, I just thought, you know what?
所以当我参加世界极限运动会（X Games）并且开始接近成功时，我当时就想，你知道吗？

922
00:33:43.090 --> 00:33:45.650
If I'm ever going to get hurt again, it'll be here.
如果我还要受伤一次，那就是在这里。

923
00:33:45.730 --> 00:33:46.090
It's here.
就是现在。

924
00:33:46.350 --> 00:33:46.610
Yeah.
是啊。

925
00:33:46.630 --> 00:33:47.230
I don't mind.
我不在乎。

926
00:33:47.530 --> 00:33:51.290
Like, I'll take one for the sake of trying to finally get it again.
就像，为了最终再次成功，我豁出去了。

927
00:33:51.290 --> 00:33:55.250
And so when I did try to land it the first time at X Games, I fell forward.
所以当我在X Games第一次尝试落地时，我向前摔倒了。

928
00:33:55.590 --> 00:33:58.350
It's all there documented, but I didn't get hurt.
这一切都有据可查，但我没有受伤。

929
00:33:58.890 --> 00:34:03.810
And that was the moment that I figured it out because I thought, if I can shift my weight
那就是我顿悟的时刻，因为我想，如果我能在旋转过程中

930
00:34:03.810 --> 00:34:06.930
mid-spin more to my back foot, I won't fall forward.
把重心更多地转移到后脚，我就不会向前摔倒了。

931
00:34:07.110 --> 00:34:10.970
And so the next attempt, I shift my weight to my back foot and then I fell backwards.
所以在下一次尝试时，我把重心转移到了后脚，结果我向后摔倒了。

932
00:34:11.730 --> 00:34:14.330
And it was like, that's the light bulb.
那种感觉就像是，灯泡亮了。

933
00:34:14.530 --> 00:34:15.390
That was the epiphany.
那就是顿悟的时刻。

934
00:34:15.770 --> 00:34:18.390
And I just had to even that balance out.
我只需要把那个平衡掌握好就行。

935
00:34:18.510 --> 00:34:18.590
Yeah.
对。

936
00:34:18.830 --> 00:34:19.610
And the next one worked.
然后下一次就成功了。

937
00:34:19.610 --> 00:34:21.950
It's really dramatic when you watch it.
你看视频的时候会觉得非常戏剧性。

938
00:34:22.050 --> 00:34:27.110
And the thing that was so moving to me is how the crowd is with you the whole entire time.
最让我感动的是，观众从头到尾都和你在一起。

939
00:34:27.110 --> 00:34:27.430
Yeah, that was wild.
对，那太疯狂了。

940
00:34:27.630 --> 00:34:28.610
I mean, I think I feel—
我是说，我觉得——

941
00:34:28.610 --> 00:34:30.510
And the other skaters are coming around.
而且其他滑手也围了过来。

942
00:34:30.650 --> 00:34:34.190
They're like almost laying hands on you and like banging their boards.
他们几乎要触碰你，还疯狂地敲击滑板。

943
00:34:34.390 --> 00:34:39.130
But I do feel like that is a slice of what skateboarding is.
但我确实觉得这正是滑板精神的缩影。

944
00:34:39.690 --> 00:34:43.910
Skateboarding is this really supportive community, even though it's an individual pursuit, even
滑板是一个非常具有支持力的群体，尽管这是一项个人追求，尽管

945
00:34:43.910 --> 00:34:45.250
though we do compete.
我们也会竞争。

946
00:34:45.710 --> 00:34:49.530
There's a brethren and there's a kindred spirit of everyone just loves.
这里有一种兄弟情谊和志同道合的精神，每个人都热爱它。

947
00:34:49.610 --> 00:34:52.310
It's doing it and loves being part of the scene.
热爱这项运动，热爱成为这个圈子的一员。

948
00:34:52.710 --> 00:34:57.990
If you go to a skate park right now, there'll be people of all ages, all races, all genders,
如果你现在去任何一个滑板公园，都会看到各个年龄、各种肤色、各种性别的人

949
00:34:58.470 --> 00:35:00.870
just enjoying the space and then cheering each other on.
都在享受这个空间，并互相加油鼓劲。

950
00:35:00.930 --> 00:35:06.850
So I just feel like that was such a great—you know, I'm honored that it was me, but whoever
所以我真的觉得这是一个绝佳的——你知道，我很荣幸那个人是我，但不管是谁

951
00:35:06.850 --> 00:35:10.370
it had been, it was a great example of what skateboarding is all about.
那真是太棒了，完美诠释了滑板运动的真谛。

952
00:35:10.950 --> 00:35:12.150
It was so beautiful.
真的太美妙了。

953
00:35:12.410 --> 00:35:17.790
I mean, after you landed it, the other skaters, they like all pile on you like you see players
我是说，在你落地之后，其他的滑手们，他们就像你看到的那样全都扑了上来，就像

954
00:35:17.790 --> 00:35:20.370
at the World Series piling on each other.
世界大赛上球员们叠罗汉那样。

955
00:35:20.750 --> 00:35:26.610
And when I watched that video, Angela, I don't know if this popped in your head, but it reminded
安吉拉，当我看了那段视频时，我不知道你脑子里有没有闪过这个念头，但这让我想起了

956
00:35:26.610 --> 00:35:30.690
me of the night that Steve Carell won the Golden Globe for playing Michael Scott.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔凭借扮演迈克尔·斯科特赢得金球奖的那天晚上。

957
00:35:30.950 --> 00:35:31.390
Oh my gosh.
哦天哪。

958
00:35:31.390 --> 00:35:32.650
That's so great.
太棒了。

959
00:35:32.750 --> 00:35:34.230
And it was totally unexpected.
而且完全出乎意料。

960
00:35:34.570 --> 00:35:36.610
We did not think he was going to win.
我们根本没想过他会赢。

961
00:35:36.750 --> 00:35:36.930
Yeah.
是的。

962
00:35:37.090 --> 00:35:37.730
And he won.
然后他赢了。

963
00:35:37.730 --> 00:35:43.430
And when he walked into the party holding that trophy, the whole cast piled onto him.
当他拿着奖杯走进派对时，整个剧组都扑到了他身上。

964
00:35:43.770 --> 00:35:44.250
That's so cool.
太酷了。

965
00:35:44.430 --> 00:35:48.930
And it was that feeling where it was like, well, I didn't win the Golden Globe.
那种感觉就像，好吧，我虽然没拿金球奖。

966
00:35:49.370 --> 00:35:49.970
But we did.
但我们赢了。

967
00:35:50.030 --> 00:35:51.810
But we won it because he won it.
我们赢了，因为他赢了。

968
00:35:51.810 --> 00:35:52.690
You would have thought, you know.
你知道的，你本会这么觉得。

969
00:35:52.970 --> 00:35:53.890
And we had emerged.
我们终于出头了。

970
00:35:53.890 --> 00:35:58.470
Yes, you won that for, you landed that for the whole community.
没错，你为这个，你为整个群体完成了那一跳。

971
00:35:58.630 --> 00:35:58.910
Yeah.
是的。

972
00:35:59.050 --> 00:35:59.930
You know, and you.
你知道的，而且你。

973
00:36:00.150 --> 00:36:01.330
It was so beautiful.
真的太美妙了。

974
00:36:01.630 --> 00:36:02.390
It's so true.
确实如此。

975
00:36:02.590 --> 00:36:06.450
We weren't even invited to the Golden Globes, the caSt.
我们剧组甚至都没有被邀请参加金球奖。

976
00:36:06.650 --> 00:36:11.910
We were in a garage parking lot annex next to the building that they had put a tent over.
我们在他们大楼旁边的车库停车场附属区里，那里搭了个帐篷。

977
00:36:12.110 --> 00:36:12.310
Wow.
哇。

978
00:36:12.450 --> 00:36:13.650
And we were with all these suits.
我们和那一帮西装革履的人在一起。

979
00:36:13.670 --> 00:36:15.310
Just watching it on like TV screens.
只能通过电视屏幕看着。

980
00:36:15.710 --> 00:36:18.790
The suits are very, the business side of the world.
那些西装革履的人，代表着商务的世界。

981
00:36:18.790 --> 00:36:21.290
And they're very sort of like, oh, you know, just sitting there proper.
他们都那种样子，你知道的，就端坐在那儿。

982
00:36:21.290 --> 00:36:26.250
And when we won, or Steve won, we lost it in this garage.
而当我们获奖，或者说史蒂夫获奖时，我们在那个车库里彻底沸腾了。

983
00:36:26.270 --> 00:36:27.650
And we were waiting for him.
我们在等他回来。

984
00:36:27.810 --> 00:36:29.630
And he let us all hold it.
他让我们所有人都拿了拿奖杯。

985
00:36:29.730 --> 00:36:32.410
I hit Phyllis in the face with it by accident in a group photo.
拍合照时我还一不小心用奖杯砸到了菲利斯的脸。

986
00:36:32.630 --> 00:36:34.350
But that's exactly what it was like.
但那感觉就跟这个一模一样。

987
00:36:34.350 --> 00:36:36.230
It felt like you won it for everybody.
感觉就像你是为每个人赢得了这个奖。

988
00:36:36.590 --> 00:36:37.390
Oh, for sure.
哦，那是肯定的。

989
00:36:37.570 --> 00:36:37.790
Yeah.
是的。

990
00:36:38.030 --> 00:36:43.510
And there was, just with that trick, there were a few of us that had been trying it for years.
而且，就那个动作而言，我们有好几个人已经尝试了好几年。

991
00:36:44.070 --> 00:36:46.770
And at some point, it was like, someone just do it already.
到某个时候，就觉得，随便谁快把这动作做出来吧。

992
00:36:46.970 --> 00:36:47.330
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

993
00:36:47.370 --> 00:36:49.770
It wasn't even like we were in competition with each other.
甚至都不是说我们在互相竞争。

994
00:36:49.770 --> 00:36:53.530
It was just like, this has to be done just so we can prove it's possible.
就只是觉得，必须得有人做出来，好证明这是可能的。

995
00:36:54.070 --> 00:36:57.350
And now it's something that young kids do.
而现在这成了小孩子们也会做的动作。

996
00:36:57.870 --> 00:36:58.670
It's wild.
太疯狂了。

997
00:36:58.870 --> 00:36:59.410
Not many.
不多。

998
00:36:59.630 --> 00:37:03.350
Not many, but it has become a little more standardized.
虽然不多，但已经变得更加规范化了。

999
00:37:03.470 --> 00:37:06.670
And also the ramps and facilities have gotten bigger.
而且坡道和设施也建得越来越大。

1000
00:37:06.910 --> 00:37:09.150
So, and there's resources, there's foam pits.
所以，现在有了各种资源，还有海绵池。

1001
00:37:09.310 --> 00:37:11.950
There's all kinds of things that you can do to work up to this.
你可以做各种各样的事情来为此做准备。

1002
00:37:12.070 --> 00:37:12.230
Yeah.
对。

1003
00:37:12.350 --> 00:37:12.450
Right.
没错。

1004
00:37:12.530 --> 00:37:14.650
I had to do it the hard way.
我是通过吃苦头才学会的。

1005
00:37:14.930 --> 00:37:15.290
The hard knocks.
饱经风霜。

1006
00:37:15.430 --> 00:37:15.490
Yeah.
对。

1007
00:37:15.710 --> 00:37:15.990
Yeah.
对。

1008
00:37:16.190 --> 00:37:17.250
Literally hard knocks.
字面意义上的吃苦头。

1009
00:37:17.770 --> 00:37:18.090
Yeah.
对。

1010
00:37:18.090 --> 00:37:22.110
I did read that if you create a trick, you get to name it.
我确实读到过，如果你自创了一个招式，你就可以给它命名。

1011
00:37:22.230 --> 00:37:22.710
Is that true?
是真的吗？

1012
00:37:23.030 --> 00:37:29.410
For the most part, it's a little tricky now because there are so many variations of moves
基本上是这样，现在稍微有点复杂了，因为动作的变化太多了

1013
00:37:29.410 --> 00:37:34.430
that it's kind of like, look, just because you did to shove it out of that, you don't
以至于有点像，听着，并不是说你从那个动作做了一个shove-it，你就能

1014
00:37:34.430 --> 00:37:34.990
get to claim that.
拥有它的署名权。

1015
00:37:35.010 --> 00:37:35.210
It doesn't mean it's yours.
这并不意味着它是你的。

1016
00:37:35.490 --> 00:37:35.610
Yeah.
对。

1017
00:37:36.030 --> 00:37:36.210
Yeah.
对。

1018
00:37:36.690 --> 00:37:37.430
But yes.
但确实如此。

1019
00:37:37.530 --> 00:37:39.910
But especially back in the day, that's where we have all these absurd names.
不过特别是过去，这就是我们拥有所有这些荒谬名称的原因。

1020
00:37:40.190 --> 00:37:40.590
Right.
没错。

1021
00:37:40.810 --> 00:37:42.150
We were looking up a few.
我们刚刚查了几个。

1022
00:37:42.670 --> 00:37:42.970
All right.
行吧。

1023
00:37:43.070 --> 00:37:44.070
Here's a question for you.
有个问题想问你。

1024
00:37:44.070 --> 00:37:50.230
Is there a skater past or present that you think maybe gets overlooked that deserves to
有没有哪个过去或现在的滑板手，你觉得可能被忽视了，但值得

1025
00:37:50.230 --> 00:37:53.550
be, have more of their story told or a legendary status?
更多地讲述他们的故事，或者享有传奇地位？

1026
00:37:54.250 --> 00:37:54.730
Yeah.
有。

1027
00:37:55.010 --> 00:37:56.150
Several for sure.
肯定的有好几个。

1028
00:37:56.710 --> 00:38:01.930
I mean, to offer a deep cut, there was a guy named David Z when Kevin and I were younger.
我的意思是，说个冷门的，我和凯文年轻时有个叫大卫·Z的家伙。

1029
00:38:02.090 --> 00:38:07.770
He was the first person we ever saw truly fly high with ease and with style, even before
他是我们见过的第一个能够真正轻松且有型地飞得很高的人，甚至在

1030
00:38:07.770 --> 00:38:08.430
Christian Osoy.
克里斯蒂安·奥索伊之前。

1031
00:38:08.790 --> 00:38:11.050
And he was just in the right place at the wrong time.
而他只是生逢不时，身处错误的时间。

1032
00:38:11.170 --> 00:38:12.890
It was just the deadest time of skating.
那是滑板运动最萧条的时期。

1033
00:38:12.890 --> 00:38:17.470
And he was a little older, so he had to find a job and just wasn't in the cards.
而且他稍微大了一点，所以他得去找工作，这就注定不行了。

1034
00:38:17.890 --> 00:38:20.150
David Z, it's even hard to find photos of him.
大卫·Z，甚至很难找到他的照片。

1035
00:38:20.490 --> 00:38:27.270
But I would say in terms of my influences, a guy named Eddie Alguera, he was the most
但如果要说对我有影响的人，有个叫埃迪·阿尔格拉的家伙，当我在滑板界

1036
00:38:27.270 --> 00:38:32.250
innovative skater when I was coming up through the ranks and people gave him a hard time
崭露头角时，他是最具创新精神的滑手，人们当时挺难为他的

1037
00:38:32.250 --> 00:38:35.430
because they said he didn't have style and he was all about tricks and he's like a robotic
因为他们说他没有风格，只专注于招式，像个机器人一样

1038
00:38:35.430 --> 00:38:39.170
and I was young and I didn't have style and I wanted to do tricks.
而我当时还年轻，也没有风格，我就想练招式。

1039
00:38:39.330 --> 00:38:40.370
So I watched everything he did.
所以我看了他做的所有事情。

1040
00:38:40.370 --> 00:38:43.230
His signature moves were my first advanced moves.
他的标志性动作成了我的第一批高级动作。

1041
00:38:43.590 --> 00:38:44.550
That's so cool.
太酷了。

1042
00:38:44.810 --> 00:38:52.030
So there were a lot of times when skateboarding went away or went out of fashion and it wasn't
所以有很多时候，滑板运动会沉寂或者过时，而且无法

1043
00:38:52.030 --> 00:38:52.710
paying the bills.
维持生计。

1044
00:38:52.970 --> 00:38:56.070
You kind of went through a lot of these droughts.
你们经历过很多这样的低谷期。

1045
00:38:56.230 --> 00:39:02.550
It really reminds me of the lifestyle of an actor where you have a show or you're doing
这真让我想起了演员的生活，你有一部剧或者你在拍

1046
00:39:02.550 --> 00:39:06.110
a movie, but then you're going to have a couple of years where you're auditioning, but you
一部电影，但接着你会有好几年一直在试镜，却

1047
00:39:06.110 --> 00:39:06.790
can't get hired.
无法被录用。

1048
00:39:07.130 --> 00:39:10.570
You had to find a lot of creative ways to stay in the business.
你们得想出很多有创意的方法来留在这一行里。

1049
00:39:10.930 --> 00:39:12.370
Can you talk a little bit about that?
你能聊聊这个吗？

1050
00:39:12.790 --> 00:39:12.870
Yeah.
可以。

1051
00:39:14.510 --> 00:39:22.930
We had a wave of success in the late 80s and we were young and naive enough to think that
我们在80年代末迎来了一波成功，当时我们年轻又天真，以为

1052
00:39:22.930 --> 00:39:24.150
that was never going to end.
这种好日子永远不会结束。

1053
00:39:24.150 --> 00:39:30.750
So we were spending as if that was happening and I had two homes.
所以我们大手大脚地花钱，仿佛那会一直持续，我当时有两栋房子。

1054
00:39:30.950 --> 00:39:35.690
I had one with these giant ramps set up and suddenly I found myself with my income kind
其中一栋搭了巨大的滑板坡道，突然间我发现自己的收入

1055
00:39:35.690 --> 00:39:40.330
of dropping by half every month because it was all royalty based and people just weren't
每个月都在减半，因为全靠版税支撑，大家不再

1056
00:39:40.330 --> 00:39:44.690
buying my skateboards or, you know, my shoe sponsor was like, oh, we got to cut your salary
买我的滑板了，或者说，你知道的，我的鞋类赞助商说，哦，我们得再削减

1057
00:39:44.690 --> 00:39:45.010
again.
你的薪水。

1058
00:39:45.310 --> 00:39:46.790
We just cut it last month.
我们上个月刚削减过。

1059
00:39:46.910 --> 00:39:47.130
Okay.
好吧。

1060
00:39:47.130 --> 00:39:51.370
And so I just did whatever I could to make ends meet.
所以我只能想方设法维持生计。

1061
00:39:51.570 --> 00:39:57.490
I, um, at one point I had a really basic editing system, which no one had, this is probably
我，嗯，有一段时间搞到了一套非常基础的剪辑系统，当时没人有这东西，大概是

1062
00:39:57.490 --> 00:39:59.370
92, 93 ish.
92或93年左右。

1063
00:39:59.530 --> 00:40:00.910
So people didn't really have that kind of stuff.
所以人们其实并没有那种设备。

1064
00:40:01.010 --> 00:40:06.230
So I just was getting odd jobs, um, editing stuff on three quarter tape.
因此我就接点零活，嗯，用四分之三英寸磁带剪辑东西。

1065
00:40:06.570 --> 00:40:06.870
Wow.
哇。

1066
00:40:07.090 --> 00:40:08.450
Not even skateboard related?
甚至都不是滑板相关的？

1067
00:40:08.690 --> 00:40:11.110
Some not skateboarding related, mostly skateboard related.
有些无关，大部分还是滑板相关的。

1068
00:40:11.530 --> 00:40:14.970
Any company that wanted to do their skate video needed to master it.
任何想做滑板视频的公司都需要母带制作。

1069
00:40:14.970 --> 00:40:17.430
They could do it in my garage and I could do it for them.
他们可以在我车库里做，我可以帮他们弄。

1070
00:40:17.750 --> 00:40:22.050
I mean, I got, you know, maybe a hundred bucks to do it or whatever it was, but I got
我的意思是，你知道的，我大概能拿个一百块钱报酬什么的，但我总算

1071
00:40:22.050 --> 00:40:23.690
by and then I started getting hired.
混了过去，然后我开始接到工作。

1072
00:40:23.890 --> 00:40:28.310
Luckily I had made enough connections in Hollywood that I started getting hired as a consultant
幸运的是，我在好莱坞建立足够多的人脉，开始受聘担任

1073
00:40:28.850 --> 00:40:36.190
on any shoot that was, that had skateboarding in it because I was 24 and considered too old
任何含有滑板元素的拍摄的顾问，因为我当时24岁，被认为年纪太大

1074
00:40:36.190 --> 00:40:37.630
to be the featured skateboarder.
而不再适合当出镜滑板手了。

1075
00:40:37.990 --> 00:40:41.770
You know, it was more, the narrative was it's for teenagers and whatever.
你知道的，当时的主流说法是滑板是给青少年玩的云云。

1076
00:40:41.770 --> 00:40:50.010
So I would go to a set and explain what is possible in whatever the landscape was.
所以我去到片场，解释在当时的场地环境下什么动作是可行的。

1077
00:40:50.130 --> 00:40:50.830
And that worked.
这招挺管用。

1078
00:40:51.010 --> 00:40:51.870
It was cool.
挺酷的。

1079
00:40:52.170 --> 00:40:55.390
I mean, I got to be in skating, but it was tricky.
我的意思是，我得以留在滑板圈里，但那确实很棘手。

1080
00:40:55.650 --> 00:40:55.830
Yeah.
是的。

1081
00:40:56.010 --> 00:40:58.670
It was, uh, there, there were some lean times.
确实，嗯，那段日子确实挺拮据的。

1082
00:40:58.690 --> 00:41:00.550
I was definitely eating a lot of Taco Bell those days.
那阵子我绝对吃了不少塔可钟。

1083
00:41:00.930 --> 00:41:01.270
Yeah.
对啊。

1084
00:41:01.330 --> 00:41:03.050
We talk about this a lot too.
我们也很经常聊到这个。

1085
00:41:03.250 --> 00:41:08.090
Like even within our careers, sometimes you just have to like see the pivot and take it,
就比如在我们的职业生涯中，有时候你必须得看到转机并抓住它

1086
00:41:08.090 --> 00:41:15.250
you know, and, and, oh, I was, I was going to fight to the death to not get a real job.
你知道的，而且，哦，我曾誓死抵抗，绝不去找一份正经工作。

1087
00:41:15.710 --> 00:41:16.110
Yeah.
对。

1088
00:41:16.590 --> 00:41:19.370
I mean, well, it's all, they are, they were real jobs.
我的意思是，其实它们也，它们以前也是正经工作。

1089
00:41:19.450 --> 00:41:23.530
I'm just talking about like just going nine to five, whatever it was like, I got to have
我只是指那种朝九晚五的生活，不管那是什么，我就觉得我得

1090
00:41:23.530 --> 00:41:24.270
something else.
做点别的。

1091
00:41:24.410 --> 00:41:24.590
Right.
没错。

1092
00:41:24.810 --> 00:41:26.590
And something still in the world of skating.
而且还要留在滑板的世界里。

1093
00:41:26.830 --> 00:41:30.650
So whatever allowed me, it really was just more, whatever allowed me to keep skating.
所以任何能让我，其实也就是，任何能让我继续滑板的事。

1094
00:41:30.790 --> 00:41:34.290
I didn't even care about being a pro or being in the magazines, whatever.
我甚至不在乎是不是职业滑手，也不在乎上不上杂志什么的。

1095
00:41:34.290 --> 00:41:35.850
I just wanted to keep skating.
我只想继续玩滑板。

1096
00:41:36.130 --> 00:41:36.270
Yeah.
对。

1097
00:41:36.450 --> 00:41:40.450
I think that's so relatable for us because all we want to do is create, you know, that's
我觉得这对我们来说太有共鸣了，因为我们唯一想做的就是创作，你知道的，那是

1098
00:41:40.450 --> 00:41:41.610
like what makes us happy.
让我们快乐的事情。

1099
00:41:41.910 --> 00:41:42.030
Right.
没错。

1100
00:41:42.150 --> 00:41:45.110
And so you just follow that wherever anyone will let you do that.
所以只要有人让你这么做，你就跟着感觉走。

1101
00:41:45.470 --> 00:41:45.790
Yeah.
对。

1102
00:41:45.910 --> 00:41:46.530
Yeah, exactly.
对，完全正确。

1103
00:41:46.750 --> 00:41:51.170
Oh, at one point, I'll tell you what, how I survived really in those days was rollerblade
哦，有那么一段时间，我跟你说，我那时候能撑下来全靠直排轮滑

1104
00:41:51.170 --> 00:41:53.430
shows because rollerblading was huge.
表演，因为当时轮滑非常火。

1105
00:41:53.610 --> 00:41:53.770
Yeah.
对。

1106
00:41:53.910 --> 00:41:54.010
Right.
没错。

1107
00:41:54.170 --> 00:41:55.250
It's the early nineties.
那是九十年代初。

1108
00:41:55.790 --> 00:41:57.930
Everyone's, you know, you saw on the street, whatever.
你知道的，大街上随处可见各种人。

1109
00:41:58.530 --> 00:42:01.130
And there were a bunch of people that skated half pipe.
有一群人在U池玩滑板。

1110
00:42:01.130 --> 00:42:06.410
And so they had these rollerblade shows all over the place, like Team Rollerblade Live,
所以到处都有这种轮滑表演，比如“轮滑之队现场秀”，

1111
00:42:06.670 --> 00:42:08.270
inline shows at Magic Mountain.
还有魔术山的直排轮滑表演。

1112
00:42:08.550 --> 00:42:13.070
And I got to be the special guest skateboarder of these shows.
我有幸成为这些表演的特邀滑板嘉宾。

1113
00:42:13.250 --> 00:42:16.050
And that paid my bills probably for a whole year.
这大概承包了我整整一年的账单。

1114
00:42:16.470 --> 00:42:16.630
Yeah.
对。

1115
00:42:17.110 --> 00:42:21.650
How do you like, how do you maintain your mental health through those droughts?
在那些事业低谷期，你是怎么维持心理健康的？

1116
00:42:21.650 --> 00:42:30.070
I think I just focused in on my strengths and realized like living the dream just morphed
我想我只是专注于自己的优势，并意识到追逐梦想只是演变成了

1117
00:42:30.070 --> 00:42:32.350
into being able to skate.
能够继续滑板。

1118
00:42:33.750 --> 00:42:38.870
So for instance, the tours before that, we were, we were flying to Europe and we had a,
所以举个例子，在那之前的巡演，我们是坐飞机去欧洲，

1119
00:42:39.010 --> 00:42:41.470
you know, we had a big van and we had these huge crowds.
你知道的，我们有一辆大货车，还有庞大的观众群体。

1120
00:42:41.470 --> 00:42:45.510
And then it became, there's six of us in our delivery van and we're all going to share
后来变成了我们六个人挤在一辆送货面包车里，还要合住

1121
00:42:45.510 --> 00:42:49.950
one room and we're going to skate whatever ramps they set up in the parking lot for us.
同一个房间，去滑他们在停车场给我们搭的各种坡道。

1122
00:42:49.950 --> 00:42:51.130
But we're still skating.
但我们依然在滑板。

1123
00:42:51.690 --> 00:42:52.090
Yeah.
对。

1124
00:42:52.250 --> 00:42:53.470
So I had to just keep it in perspective.
所以我必须摆正心态。

1125
00:42:54.210 --> 00:42:55.650
And yeah, it sucked.
而且说实话，这真的很烂。

1126
00:42:55.770 --> 00:42:58.290
It was hot and I was rolling my ankles left and right.
天气很热，我的脚踝左右两侧频繁扭伤。

1127
00:42:58.470 --> 00:43:02.490
And I'm in charge, like I'm only 25 and I'm in charge.
而且我得负责，我当时才25岁就要负责任。

1128
00:43:02.690 --> 00:43:08.890
Like I'm the tour manager of this chaos, you know, but all along we got to skate.
就像我是这场混乱的巡演经理一样，你知道的，但一路上我们还能滑板。

1129
00:43:09.150 --> 00:43:11.450
And so that's how I kept my mental health in check.
所以这就是我保持心理健康的方式。

1130
00:43:11.690 --> 00:43:14.830
If I was unable to skate, then I would start kind of losing it.
如果我没法滑板，我大概就要崩溃了。

1131
00:43:15.370 --> 00:43:21.170
I think it's pretty amazing what your game has brought to the skating community as well.
我觉得你的游戏对滑板界贡献巨大，这真的很了不起。

1132
00:43:21.370 --> 00:43:26.830
So my sons, they don't know how to skateboard, but they love your games.
所以我的儿子们，他们不会玩滑板，但他们超爱你的游戏。

1133
00:43:27.010 --> 00:43:27.790
Oh, so cool.
哦，太酷了。

1134
00:43:27.830 --> 00:43:29.750
They love Tony Hawk Pro Skater.
他们超爱《托尼·霍克职业滑板》。

1135
00:43:29.870 --> 00:43:32.690
And they were so excited that I was meeting you today.
他们听说我今天要见你，兴奋得不得了。

1136
00:43:32.830 --> 00:43:35.510
And we meet like really great people all the time.
我们平时也经常遇到一些很厉害的大人物。

1137
00:43:35.650 --> 00:43:37.010
And they're like, oh yeah, that's cool.
他们就会说，哦，好吧，那挺酷的。

1138
00:43:37.090 --> 00:43:38.030
And I said your name.
但当我提到你的名字时。

1139
00:43:38.110 --> 00:43:39.290
They're like, no way.
他们的反应是，不会吧。

1140
00:43:39.950 --> 00:43:41.470
And they were like, are you serious?
他们会说，你是认真的吗？

1141
00:43:41.710 --> 00:43:45.890
And I guess you have a big game that's coming out July 11th, like the three and four.
我猜你有一款大作要在7月11日发售，就是那个三代和四代合集。

1142
00:43:46.090 --> 00:43:46.790
They told me.
他们告诉我的。

1143
00:43:47.470 --> 00:43:48.190
So that's...
所以这就……

1144
00:43:48.190 --> 00:43:48.430
Wow.
哇。

1145
00:43:48.570 --> 00:43:50.550
So they did my own press for me.
所以他们帮我把宣传工作都做了。

1146
00:43:50.630 --> 00:43:50.990
Thank you.
谢谢。

1147
00:43:51.370 --> 00:43:53.250
They were like, no, there's a new game coming out.
他们当时说，不对，有新游戏要出了。

1148
00:43:53.250 --> 00:43:54.170
They have my talking points.
他们连我的宣传要点都知道。

1149
00:43:54.210 --> 00:43:54.770
They do.
确实如此。

1150
00:43:55.190 --> 00:43:56.750
I went and looked up the date.
我自己还特意去查了发售日期。

1151
00:43:56.870 --> 00:43:59.230
They didn't know the date, but they're like, no, there's a new one coming out.
他们不知道具体日期，但他们觉得，不，有一款新的要出来了。

1152
00:43:59.470 --> 00:43:59.690
Yeah.
是啊。

1153
00:43:59.750 --> 00:44:02.650
Hey, just the fact that they know that is a big deal to me.
嘿，光是他们知道这一点，对我就已经很了不起了。

1154
00:44:03.030 --> 00:44:03.390
Yeah?
是吗？

1155
00:44:03.650 --> 00:44:03.910
Yeah.
对。

1156
00:44:04.030 --> 00:44:08.270
Because we've been working for a while on that and it's been really hard to contain the secrets.
因为我们为此努力了一段时间，要保守秘密真的很艰难。

1157
00:44:08.270 --> 00:44:10.730
So we finally got to reveal it last week.
所以我们上周终于得以将其揭晓。

1158
00:44:10.970 --> 00:44:11.770
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

1159
00:44:11.910 --> 00:44:12.050
Yeah.
是啊。

1160
00:44:12.270 --> 00:44:12.430
Yeah.
对。

1161
00:44:12.510 --> 00:44:12.950
No, they know.
不，他们知道。

1162
00:44:13.050 --> 00:44:14.830
I think they follow gamers, you know?
我觉得他们关注了游戏玩家，你知道吧？

1163
00:44:14.930 --> 00:44:15.110
Okay.
好吧。

1164
00:44:15.110 --> 00:44:16.590
And so when things are announced...
所以当有消息公布时……

1165
00:44:16.590 --> 00:44:17.670
Yeah, we did an event.
对，我们办了一场活动。

1166
00:44:17.810 --> 00:44:19.110
A lot of influencers were there.
很多网红都在现场。

1167
00:44:19.270 --> 00:44:21.130
A lot of the bands that are featured in the game were there.
游戏中收录的很多乐队也在现场。

1168
00:44:21.610 --> 00:44:24.030
A lot of the characters that are featured in the game were there.
游戏中登场的很多角色也在现场。

1169
00:44:24.270 --> 00:44:26.070
So I'm glad it came across their radar.
所以我很高兴它进入了他们的视线。

1170
00:44:26.510 --> 00:44:26.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1171
00:44:27.470 --> 00:44:29.730
Can you say some of the bands that were there?
你能说出到场的其中一些乐队吗？

1172
00:44:30.090 --> 00:44:30.390
Sure.
当然。

1173
00:44:31.410 --> 00:44:32.890
Urethane is one of the bands.
Urethane 是其中一个乐队。

1174
00:44:33.550 --> 00:44:35.650
Steve Caballero is pro skater is actually in that band.
职业滑板选手史蒂夫·卡巴列罗其实就在那个乐队里。

1175
00:44:35.650 --> 00:44:36.090
Uh-huh.
呃哼。

1176
00:44:36.270 --> 00:44:40.850
The Adolescents, who did songs like Amoeba and Kids of the Black Hole.
The Adolescents，他们创作了像《Amoeba》和《Kids of the Black Hole》这样的歌曲。

1177
00:44:41.350 --> 00:44:43.890
You've heard them, but you probably don't know what that is.
你听过，但你可能不知道那是什么。

1178
00:44:44.490 --> 00:44:47.170
Danny Brown is a hip-hop artist from Detroit.
丹尼·布朗是来自底特律的嘻哈艺术家。

1179
00:44:47.450 --> 00:44:51.770
And Lupe Fiasco, who famously has the Kick Push song about skateboarding.
还有卢佩·菲亚斯科，他以那首关于滑板的著名歌曲《Kick Push》而闻名。

1180
00:44:52.070 --> 00:44:57.350
I just know how much music is a part of the skateboarding culture as well.
我只是很清楚音乐在滑板文化中同样占据着多么重要的部分。

1181
00:44:57.570 --> 00:45:00.730
I was telling you that my very first boyfriend was a skateboarder.
我之前跟你说过，我的初恋男友是个滑板手。

1182
00:45:00.730 --> 00:45:06.870
Yes, my high school love of my life, and I spent two or three years at skate parks.
对，我高中时的挚爱，我在滑板公园度过了两三年。

1183
00:45:06.870 --> 00:45:07.250
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

1184
00:45:07.390 --> 00:45:08.110
Watching him skate.
看着他滑板。

1185
00:45:08.550 --> 00:45:09.310
St. Louis.
圣路易斯。

1186
00:45:09.810 --> 00:45:10.110
Okay.
好吧。

1187
00:45:10.310 --> 00:45:11.270
I was a skate betty.
我曾是个滑板辣妹。

1188
00:45:11.610 --> 00:45:13.730
I don't know if we're still allowed to call ourselves skate betty.
我不知道我们现在是不是还能自称滑板辣妹。

1189
00:45:13.730 --> 00:45:14.390
That's pretty cool.
那挺酷的。

1190
00:45:14.770 --> 00:45:15.470
That's OG.
那很元老级。

1191
00:45:16.570 --> 00:45:17.290
That's right.
没错。

1192
00:45:17.990 --> 00:45:20.830
I wore the t-shirts and dressed in the gear.
我穿 T 恤，穿着全套装备。

1193
00:45:21.070 --> 00:45:23.030
When you say you wore the t-shirts, what does that mean?
当你指穿着 T 恤时，那是什么意思？

1194
00:45:23.030 --> 00:45:29.790
Like a Thrasher t-shirt or like this, you know, Black Flag t-shirt.
就像 Thrasher 的 T 恤，或者像这个，你知道的，Black Flag 的 T 恤。

1195
00:45:30.370 --> 00:45:32.550
Yeah, Black Flag, World Industries.
对，Black Flag，World Industries。

1196
00:45:33.050 --> 00:45:34.290
I don't remember.
我记不清了。

1197
00:45:34.670 --> 00:45:34.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1198
00:45:35.050 --> 00:45:35.550
What years?
那是哪几年？

1199
00:45:36.350 --> 00:45:37.910
I would have been there.
我当时应该也在那儿。

1200
00:45:37.910 --> 00:45:42.090
So this, I guess, which I didn't realize in St. Louis, Missouri, nobody told us there
所以这个，我想，我在密苏里州圣路易斯时居然没意识到，没人告诉过我们

1201
00:45:42.090 --> 00:45:46.030
was a skateboarding drought during like 88 to 91.
大约在88到91年期间，滑板运动经历了一段低谷。

1202
00:45:46.310 --> 00:45:46.470
Yeah.
是啊。

1203
00:45:46.750 --> 00:45:48.770
I mean, we were like, it was in full force.
我的意思是，我们当时觉得，它正处于全盛时期。

1204
00:45:48.770 --> 00:45:54.470
And all these guys would go out there on the half pipe and they'd be trying to do the stuff.
所有这些家伙都会去U型槽那里尝试各种动作。

1205
00:45:54.730 --> 00:45:57.230
Did you ever go to a half pipe that was plexiglass?
你有没有去过有机玻璃做的U型槽？

1206
00:45:57.790 --> 00:45:58.330
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

1207
00:45:58.570 --> 00:46:00.990
I don't think so.
我想我没有。

1208
00:46:01.150 --> 00:46:01.610
In St. Louis?
在圣路易斯？

1209
00:46:01.810 --> 00:46:01.890
No.
没有。

1210
00:46:02.130 --> 00:46:06.250
Because there was a half pipe in St. Louis that was portable that I skated many times in those years.
因为圣路易斯有一个可移动的U型槽，我在那些年里滑过很多次。

1211
00:46:07.270 --> 00:46:07.670
Wow.
哇。

1212
00:46:07.730 --> 00:46:08.810
I don't think so.
我不觉得我有。

1213
00:46:08.890 --> 00:46:10.130
I think I would have remembered that.
我想我应该会记得那个。

1214
00:46:10.810 --> 00:46:16.650
One of the parks we went to was, I guess, is this called a bowl where it's cement?
我们去过的其中一个公园，我猜，这种水泥砌成的叫碗池吗？

1215
00:46:16.970 --> 00:46:17.110
Yep.
对。

1216
00:46:17.110 --> 00:46:22.550
And then there were other like wooden half pipes or quarter pipes or whatever.
然后还有其他像是木制的U型槽、四分之一管状池什么的。

1217
00:46:23.110 --> 00:46:23.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1218
00:46:23.490 --> 00:46:26.690
I mean, and it was, I loved those guys.
我的意思是，而且，我真的很喜欢那些家伙。

1219
00:46:26.790 --> 00:46:26.990
Yep.
没错。

1220
00:46:27.350 --> 00:46:27.730
Like.
比如。

1221
00:46:27.970 --> 00:46:28.970
Really creative.
真的很有创意。

1222
00:46:29.230 --> 00:46:29.990
Good guys.
人很好。

1223
00:46:30.310 --> 00:46:30.370
Yeah.
对。

1224
00:46:30.650 --> 00:46:31.970
Just kind of doing their own thing.
就是那种做自己事情的人。

1225
00:46:32.130 --> 00:46:32.530
Yes.
是的。

1226
00:46:32.670 --> 00:46:34.070
And not caring what anyone thinks.
而且不在乎别人怎么想。

1227
00:46:34.450 --> 00:46:34.810
No.
对。

1228
00:46:35.030 --> 00:46:39.730
And it made me want to ask you, what part of skateboarding culture do you think has been
这让我想问你，你觉得滑板文化的哪个部分

1229
00:46:39.730 --> 00:46:42.950
most misunderstood or misrepresented by the mainstream?
最容易被主流社会误解或歪曲？

1230
00:46:43.510 --> 00:46:50.990
Um, I think it's more the, the misfit aspect in that they want to focus on these are outcasts
嗯，我觉得主要是那种格格不入的方面，他们总想把这些人当成

1231
00:46:50.990 --> 00:46:52.050
or that they're troublemakers.
被排挤者或是捣蛋鬼。

1232
00:46:52.050 --> 00:46:56.230
And it's like, no, they just, they're just doing their own thing and they're doing it
但实际上并非如此，他们只是在做自己的事情，并且

1233
00:46:56.230 --> 00:46:57.510
in a highly creative way.
用一种极具创意的方式来完成。

1234
00:46:57.510 --> 00:47:04.330
And I feel like skateboarding teaches you so much about how to solve problems, how to be
我觉得滑板教会了你很多关于如何解决问题、如何做到

1235
00:47:04.330 --> 00:47:09.550
self-motivated and instill self-confidence, like maybe nothing else in your life.
自我驱动以及树立自信的道理，这是生活中其他事情可能无法比拟的。

1236
00:47:09.650 --> 00:47:14.070
And it makes you see, it's just as great equalizer, but it's very inclusive.
它让你看到，它既是一个伟大的平衡器，又具有很强的包容性。

1237
00:47:14.070 --> 00:47:17.510
So you just get to hang out with all kinds of different people, but you have the shared
所以你可以和各种各样的人一起玩，但你们有着共同的

1238
00:47:17.510 --> 00:47:19.650
interest and an immediate bond.
兴趣和瞬间建立的羁绊。

1239
00:47:19.650 --> 00:47:21.070
I totally agree.
我完全同意。

1240
00:47:21.370 --> 00:47:27.530
And I think like, I mean, I know that when I brought my skateboarding boyfriend home for
而且我觉得，我的意思是，我知道当我把带有着一头蓝发的

1241
00:47:27.530 --> 00:47:33.810
the first time with his like blue hair and, um, his like crazy way that he dressed and
滑板男友第一次带回家时，嗯，他那种疯狂的穿衣风格，还有

1242
00:47:33.810 --> 00:47:36.310
his like, you know, slouchy clothes and all this stuff.
他那种松垮的衣服之类的东西。

1243
00:47:36.750 --> 00:47:40.490
I know that my parents were a little bit like, huh?
我知道我父母当时有点儿……啊？

1244
00:47:40.730 --> 00:47:40.970
Yep.
没错。

1245
00:47:41.350 --> 00:47:41.730
Okay.
好吧。

1246
00:47:41.950 --> 00:47:42.250
Okay.
好吧。

1247
00:47:42.330 --> 00:47:47.050
Cause I was going to like a private Catholic girl's school and, you know, they would always
因为我当时在上一所私立天主教女子学校，你知道的，他们总是

1248
00:47:47.050 --> 00:47:50.370
be mixers with the private boys schools and all that.
会和私立男子学校举办联谊会之类的。

1249
00:47:50.510 --> 00:47:53.950
Like those were the like dances that you were encouraged to go to.
就像那是鼓励你去参加的舞会一样。

1250
00:47:54.190 --> 00:47:59.230
And, and I was like, I don't know what to tell you guys, but you know, those prep school
然后，我当时就想，我不知道该怎么跟你们说，但你知道，那些预科学校的

1251
00:47:59.230 --> 00:48:01.290
boys, they got nothing on the skater boys.
男生们，他们在滑板男孩面前简直不值一提。

1252
00:48:01.350 --> 00:48:08.230
Like they are it because also the skaters were not slackers or delinquents or any of that.
就好像他们才是王道，因为滑板手既不是懒虫，也不是太保，完全不是那回事。

1253
00:48:08.470 --> 00:48:09.070
They're disciplined.
他们很有纪律。

1254
00:48:09.290 --> 00:48:09.410
Yeah.
对啊。

1255
00:48:09.530 --> 00:48:10.230
Very disciplined.
非常有纪律。

1256
00:48:10.470 --> 00:48:14.930
I mean, listen, if you want to date a skater, be prepared to sit at a skate park for like
我是说，听着，如果你想跟滑板手约会，做好在滑板公园一坐就是

1257
00:48:14.930 --> 00:48:17.550
hours watching them try a trick because.
几个小时的准备，看着他们尝试一个招式，因为。

1258
00:48:17.890 --> 00:48:18.630
And nursing wounds.
还得照顾伤口。

1259
00:48:18.850 --> 00:48:19.250
Yes.
没错。

1260
00:48:19.490 --> 00:48:22.730
I mean, a couple of broken wrists and things.
我是说，会有几次骨折和诸如此类的事。

1261
00:48:22.890 --> 00:48:23.030
Yep.
没错。

1262
00:48:23.410 --> 00:48:25.910
Not just from falling, but from like a board hitting.
不只是因为摔倒，还因为比如滑板砸到。

1263
00:48:26.130 --> 00:48:28.990
I mean, that was how my boyfriend broke his wrist was like his board flipped up and then
我是说，我男友就是这么骨折的，当时他的滑板翻起来，然后

1264
00:48:28.990 --> 00:48:30.210
cranked him in the wriSt.
狠狠抽了他的手腕。

1265
00:48:30.430 --> 00:48:30.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1266
00:48:30.890 --> 00:48:31.470
That's rough.
太惨了。

1267
00:48:31.590 --> 00:48:33.310
That is, that's literally insult to injury.
真的，这简直是伤口上撒盐。

1268
00:48:33.550 --> 00:48:36.050
It really, really is.
真的，确实如此。

1269
00:48:36.370 --> 00:48:36.670
Yeah.
对啊。

1270
00:48:36.830 --> 00:48:38.750
So I just, I think it's a cool thing.
所以我只是，我觉得这是一件很酷的事。

1271
00:48:38.830 --> 00:48:43.230
And I, and I think that it's really, really cool that through your foundation, you have the
而且我，而且我觉得通过你的基金会，做滑板公园项目

1272
00:48:43.230 --> 00:48:49.850
skate park project where you have helped fund something like over 600 skate parks around
真的很酷，你们资助了全球

1273
00:48:49.850 --> 00:48:50.250
the world.
600多个滑板公园。

1274
00:48:50.530 --> 00:48:51.290
One in St. Louis actually.
其实圣路易斯就有一个。

1275
00:48:51.530 --> 00:48:51.870
And one in St. Louis.
圣路易斯也有一个。

1276
00:48:51.870 --> 00:48:52.330
A couple years ago.
几年前。

1277
00:48:52.450 --> 00:48:52.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1278
00:48:52.890 --> 00:48:53.850
That is so cool.
太酷了。

1279
00:48:53.970 --> 00:48:54.090
Yeah.
对啊。

1280
00:48:54.110 --> 00:48:55.130
I got to go to the grand opening of that one.
我有幸去参加了那个滑板公园的盛大开幕。

1281
00:48:55.210 --> 00:48:55.450
It was cool.
真的很酷。

1282
00:48:55.670 --> 00:48:56.410
That's so great.
太棒了。

1283
00:48:56.450 --> 00:48:56.590
Yep.
没错。

1284
00:48:56.850 --> 00:49:02.490
Well, I'm a dinosaur because I'm going to just tell you that I, I grew up roller skating.
好吧，我真是个老古董了，因为我要告诉你们，我，我是玩轮滑长大的。

1285
00:49:02.930 --> 00:49:04.070
Like I still roller skate.
就像我到现在还在玩轮滑。

1286
00:49:04.210 --> 00:49:04.730
My roller skates.
我的轮滑鞋。

1287
00:49:05.010 --> 00:49:05.060
Quads.
双排轮的。

1288
00:49:05.810 --> 00:49:06.190
Yes.
对。

1289
00:49:06.330 --> 00:49:06.470
Yeah.
是啊。

1290
00:49:06.690 --> 00:49:07.110
Old school.
老派风格。

1291
00:49:07.310 --> 00:49:07.630
Quads are cool, man.
双排轮滑鞋很酷的，老兄。

1292
00:49:07.790 --> 00:49:08.010
Yeah.
对啊。

1293
00:49:08.150 --> 00:49:09.110
I grew up in Indonesia.
我在印度尼西亚长大。

1294
00:49:09.370 --> 00:49:11.790
So like I got my first pair through the Sears catalog.
所以我的第一双鞋是通过西尔斯百货目录买的。

1295
00:49:11.790 --> 00:49:17.330
It took six months to get there, but you know, the pair I still skate with, I have three pairs
花了我六个月才寄到，不过你知道的，我现在还在穿的那双，我家大门前

1296
00:49:17.330 --> 00:49:18.010
by the front door.
放着三双轮滑鞋。

1297
00:49:18.190 --> 00:49:25.970
I got in Redondo beach in like 94, but they're still my favorite, but there are skate parks
我大约94年在雷东多海滩买的，但它们依然是我的最爱，不过有些滑板公园

1298
00:49:25.970 --> 00:49:29.350
that have the smaller, like little Hills and stuff like that.
有比较小的那种小土坡之类的地方。

1299
00:49:29.470 --> 00:49:35.230
And we would go and try to do, you know, whatever, just pop back on your back four, jump
然后我们会去尝试，你知道的，随便做点什么，后退着用四个轮子着地，或者

1300
00:49:35.230 --> 00:49:37.230
a little thing, like really small things.
从小土坡上跳过去，都是非常小的坡。

1301
00:49:37.230 --> 00:49:40.370
But it was such a way to de-stress for me.
但对我来说，这真是一种很好的减压方式。

1302
00:49:40.570 --> 00:49:41.370
And it still is.
现在依然如此。

1303
00:49:41.530 --> 00:49:43.010
And I have outdoor wheels.
而且我有户外轮子。

1304
00:49:43.230 --> 00:49:43.950
Those are my favorite.
那些是我的最爱。

1305
00:49:44.210 --> 00:49:46.110
I don't really like indoor skating as much.
我其实没那么喜欢室内滑冰。

1306
00:49:46.270 --> 00:49:48.090
It's, I like to be outside.
就是，我喜欢待在户外。

1307
00:49:48.130 --> 00:49:50.070
Outdoor, they're more like skateboard wheels.
在户外，它们更像是滑板轮。

1308
00:49:50.410 --> 00:49:50.910
They're bigger.
它们更大。

1309
00:49:51.150 --> 00:49:55.710
And, um, but I just find it as a way to just sort of check out of my mind and get into
而且，嗯，我只是觉得这是一种能让我放空大脑、专注于

1310
00:49:55.710 --> 00:49:56.150
my body.
身体的方式。

1311
00:49:56.430 --> 00:50:00.530
I mean, that's, that's why I continue to do it against all odds and through injuries.
我的意思是，这就是为什么我排除万难、带伤也要坚持下去的原因。

1312
00:50:00.830 --> 00:50:01.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1313
00:50:01.070 --> 00:50:02.870
That's my, that's my Zen for sure.
那绝对是我的精神宁静之地。

1314
00:50:02.870 --> 00:50:03.810
But I think it's cool.
不过我觉得这很酷。

1315
00:50:03.910 --> 00:50:06.130
You do quads or they're making a huge comeback.
你玩的是双排轮滑吗？它们现在卷土重来，大受欢迎。

1316
00:50:06.450 --> 00:50:10.990
There's quite a faction of young girls that are starting to do quad skating at skate parks
如今有一大批年轻女孩开始在滑板公园里玩双排轮滑

1317
00:50:10.990 --> 00:50:11.410
these days.
了。

1318
00:50:11.730 --> 00:50:17.390
Well, I almost brought him in today and my husband was like, no, don't meet Tony on
其实我差点今天把它带过来，但我丈夫说，别，别踩着

1319
00:50:17.390 --> 00:50:17.990
roller skates.
轮滑鞋去见托尼。

1320
00:50:18.130 --> 00:50:18.830
That's too dorky.
那太傻气了。

1321
00:50:18.850 --> 00:50:19.450
No, I love it.
不，我喜欢。

1322
00:50:21.150 --> 00:50:22.450
I've got another question.
我还有另一个问题。

1323
00:50:22.770 --> 00:50:27.330
What life skills does skateboarding build that you can't learn in a classroom?
滑板培养了哪些在课堂上学不到的生活技能？

1324
00:50:27.330 --> 00:50:36.570
Yeah, I think, uh, discipline in a way that is much more intense and much more self projected
对，我觉得，呃，这种纪律性要强烈得多，也更具自发性，

1325
00:50:37.050 --> 00:50:40.010
where it's not someone telling you, you got to do this, do these reps.
不是别人告诉你‘你必须做这个，做这些动作重复’。

1326
00:50:40.250 --> 00:50:42.030
It's like, you know, you just got to get up and try.
而是，你知道的，你必须自己站起来去尝试。

1327
00:50:42.410 --> 00:50:45.310
You just got to keep trying and getting up and persistence.
你必须不断尝试、不断站起来，这就是坚持不懈。

1328
00:50:45.830 --> 00:50:50.270
And I think, I think probably the, the one thing skating taught me through all my years
而且我认为，多年来滑板教给我的最重要的

1329
00:50:50.270 --> 00:50:54.250
is to embrace failure because that's how I'm going to learn.
一件事就是拥抱失败，因为那是我的学习方式。

1330
00:50:54.390 --> 00:50:56.130
And that's how I'm going to figure these other things out.
这也是我弄懂其他事情的方式。

1331
00:50:56.130 --> 00:51:02.890
And, and even like breaking my rib, doing 900, I am glad I did that because that led me to
甚至像做900度转体摔断肋骨那样的事，我也很高兴自己经历了，因为这让我

1332
00:51:02.890 --> 00:51:07.290
actually figure the whole thing out, put, put a stall in my efforts a little bit, but
真正把整件事琢磨透了，虽然让我的努力稍微停滞了一下，但

1333
00:51:07.290 --> 00:51:08.470
it's more like that.
情况更像是这样。

1334
00:51:08.630 --> 00:51:16.810
It's that you needed those failures to either learn or to keep yourself in reality because
你需要那些失败来学习，或者让你保持清醒面对现实，因为

1335
00:51:16.810 --> 00:51:17.910
not everything's going to win.
并非所有事情都能成功。

1336
00:51:19.150 --> 00:51:20.670
Not every show is going to be the office.
不是每部剧都能成为《办公室》。

1337
00:51:21.330 --> 00:51:22.490
Tell me about it.
可不是嘛。

1338
00:51:22.830 --> 00:51:24.010
No, no show is going to be the office.
不，没有任何剧能成为《办公室》。

1339
00:51:24.570 --> 00:51:30.770
I mean, our overnight success was each of us about nine years, nine years of just out there,
我是说，我们的一夜成名其实各自经历了大约九年，整整九年的摸爬滚打，

1340
00:51:30.950 --> 00:51:32.390
just doing anything we could.
只要能做的事我们都去尝试。

1341
00:51:32.690 --> 00:51:33.370
So great.
太棒了。

1342
00:51:33.630 --> 00:51:33.770
Yeah.
是啊。

1343
00:51:34.370 --> 00:51:35.710
Well, this has just been so great.
嗯，这次访谈真的太棒了。

1344
00:51:35.810 --> 00:51:38.310
Is there anything you want to ask us the office related?
有什么关于《办公室》的问题想问我们的吗？

1345
00:51:38.870 --> 00:51:39.330
Yeah.
有。

1346
00:51:39.430 --> 00:51:45.130
I mean, what, what is it like to, I just can't think of any other TV shows barring,
我是说，那种感觉是怎样的？我简直想不出还有哪部电视剧，除了

1347
00:51:45.130 --> 00:51:49.530
say the Simpsons or, you know, something that happened in the seventies or eight, like cheers.
比如《辛普森一家》或者你知道的七八十年代播出的剧，像《干杯》那种。

1348
00:51:50.270 --> 00:51:52.290
What's it like to have a TV show that's so iconic?
拥有一部如此具有标志性的电视剧是什么感觉？

1349
00:51:52.410 --> 00:51:54.110
It is, it's a meme factory.
确实，它简直是个表情包工厂。

1350
00:51:54.550 --> 00:51:54.970
Yeah.
对啊。

1351
00:51:55.650 --> 00:51:56.070
Still.
依然。

1352
00:51:56.550 --> 00:51:56.850
Yeah.
对。

1353
00:51:56.850 --> 00:51:59.750
I get sent myself all the time.
我自己也经常被发到网上。

1354
00:51:59.990 --> 00:52:00.070
To you people.
发给你们这样的人。

1355
00:52:00.430 --> 00:52:04.210
But is it hard for you guys to exist in the real world in that sense?
但从这个意义上说，你们在现实世界中生存会很难吗？

1356
00:52:04.670 --> 00:52:07.670
It is not hard for me to exist in the real world.
我在现实世界中生存并不难。

1357
00:52:07.670 --> 00:52:14.650
I feel like I have such an identity outside of that job and outside of the fame of that job.
我觉得除了那份工作以及那份工作带来的名气之外，我有很强的自我认同感。

1358
00:52:14.910 --> 00:52:23.770
And I'm so grateful because I love to travel, that I can go to any kind of like iconic sort of like tourist attraction.
我非常感激，因为我喜欢旅行，我可以去任何那种标志性的、类似旅游景点的敌方。

1359
00:52:24.250 --> 00:52:29.170
And I don't get like overly recognized or bothered or anything.
而且我不会被过度认出、打扰或者怎么样。

1360
00:52:29.170 --> 00:52:31.110
Like I can go up in the Eiffel Tower.
比如我可以登上埃菲尔铁塔。

1361
00:52:31.290 --> 00:52:36.650
Like I think of like, can Taylor Swift, she can't just go up in the Eiffel Tower, right?
比如我想，泰勒·斯威夫特能直接登上埃菲尔铁塔吗？她不能，对吧？

1362
00:52:36.650 --> 00:52:40.150
Or Jennifer Aniston can't just go up in the Eiffel Tower if she's in Paris.
或者詹妮弗·安妮斯顿如果在巴黎，也不能直接登上埃菲尔铁塔。

1363
00:52:40.530 --> 00:52:44.970
And so I feel so grateful that I can do those things.
所以我感到非常感激，我能做这些事情。

1364
00:52:44.970 --> 00:52:46.950
You can lead a relatively normal life.
你能过上相对正常的生活。

1365
00:52:46.990 --> 00:52:47.370
I can.
我可以。

1366
00:52:47.470 --> 00:52:48.150
I can.
我可以。

1367
00:52:48.470 --> 00:52:50.030
And so I, and I do.
所以我也确实这么做了。

1368
00:52:50.670 --> 00:52:51.070
Yeah.
对。

1369
00:52:51.290 --> 00:52:56.230
To me, it's just all like abundant universe kind of stuff, you know?
对我来说，这就像是宇宙的恩赐之类的，你知道吗？

1370
00:52:56.350 --> 00:52:59.770
It's just, I look back on it and I'm like, wow, that was so cool.
我回首往事时就会觉得，哇，那太酷了。

1371
00:53:00.090 --> 00:53:01.870
I'm so glad I got to do that.
我很高兴我能经历这一切。

1372
00:53:02.010 --> 00:53:05.830
And then I'm so grateful that I get to continue just working with my best friend.
而且我很庆幸自己能继续和最好的朋友一起工作。

1373
00:53:05.830 --> 00:53:09.330
And, and we journeyed a lot of that together.
而且，我们一起经历了很多那样的旅程。

1374
00:53:09.330 --> 00:53:18.490
And that's been a huge amount of support because we started the office and traveled through becoming famous together.
这给了我巨大的支持，因为我们一起创立了《办公室》，又一起经历了成名的过程。

1375
00:53:18.650 --> 00:53:22.870
So having a core group of people that have known you for a really long time.
所以拥有一个认识你很久的核心朋友圈子。

1376
00:53:23.090 --> 00:53:26.770
My best friends in LA are still my friends, Michael and Tobias.
我在洛杉矶最好的朋友依然是迈克尔和托拜厄斯。

1377
00:53:26.770 --> 00:53:29.350
We were operators at 1-800-DENTISTS together.
我们曾经一起在 1-800-DENTISTS 做接线员。

1378
00:53:29.690 --> 00:53:30.070
Wow.
哇。

1379
00:53:30.510 --> 00:53:32.890
Before, you know, that's what I did.
在我知道之前，那就是我的工作。

1380
00:53:32.990 --> 00:53:35.430
I did that and I did shows at improv theaters.
我做过那个，还演过即兴喜剧。

1381
00:53:35.750 --> 00:53:39.570
And to have that community that has known you that long is so important.
拥有一个认识你那么久的社群是非常重要的。

1382
00:53:39.830 --> 00:53:43.330
And then I just, I like people and I like meeting people that love the office.
然后我就是，我喜欢人，也喜欢结识那些喜欢《办公室》的人。

1383
00:53:43.510 --> 00:53:46.030
It makes me happy that they're still connecting to it.
看到他们依然和这部剧保持着连接，我很高兴。

1384
00:53:46.110 --> 00:53:47.770
Like you and your daughter, like that's so cool.
就像你和你的女儿一样，这太酷了。

1385
00:53:47.890 --> 00:53:48.470
I love that.
我太喜欢了。

1386
00:53:48.650 --> 00:53:50.090
Are you guys ever over it?
你们会觉得厌烦吗？

1387
00:53:50.790 --> 00:53:51.390
I don't think.
我想不会。

1388
00:53:51.390 --> 00:53:54.610
I mean, I, we were doing a podcast based on it, so I'm seeing the answer is no.
我是说，我，我们一直在做一档基于它的播客，所以我的回答是不会。

1389
00:53:54.950 --> 00:53:56.790
No, I mean, yeah.
不，我是说，对。

1390
00:53:56.790 --> 00:54:02.010
I mean, and you know, sometimes you get like, I've seen like snarky comments on my Instagram
我是说，你知道，有时你会收到，我看到过我 Instagram 上有些尖酸的评论

1391
00:54:02.010 --> 00:54:04.950
or something where someone's like, get over it.
或者别的什么，有人会说，放手吧。

1392
00:54:05.050 --> 00:54:06.050
It was a long time ago.
那是很久以前的事了。

1393
00:54:06.150 --> 00:54:08.310
Like you still are talking about this thing.
就像你还在谈论这件事。

1394
00:54:08.510 --> 00:54:10.090
Projecting their own failures on you.
把他们自己的失败投射到你身上。

1395
00:54:10.250 --> 00:54:15.810
Well, I mean, my feeling is like, oh, I'm sorry, but I kind of did a super cool thing.
嗯，我的感觉是，哦，我很抱歉，但我确实做了一件超级酷的事。

1396
00:54:15.810 --> 00:54:18.190
And I'm never getting tired of it.
而且我永远都不会对它感到厌倦。

1397
00:54:18.310 --> 00:54:19.950
Like, it was awesome.
真的太棒了。

1398
00:54:20.250 --> 00:54:20.570
Yeah.
对。

1399
00:54:20.630 --> 00:54:20.990
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1400
00:54:21.090 --> 00:54:21.770
I'm, are you kidding me?
我，你是在开玩笑吗？

1401
00:54:21.810 --> 00:54:23.250
I'm, I'm milking it to the end.
我真的是，把这个热度榨干到最后一刻。

1402
00:54:23.710 --> 00:54:23.970
Yeah.
对。

1403
00:54:24.450 --> 00:54:24.710
Absolutely.
绝对的。

1404
00:54:24.910 --> 00:54:28.390
And I think, I think, I think, I think that's what smart people do.
而且我觉得，我觉得，我觉得，我觉得聪明人就是这么做的。

1405
00:54:28.530 --> 00:54:32.450
They find their thing and then they lean the fuck into it as hard as they can.
他们找到自己的专长，然后拼尽全力去死磕到底。

1406
00:54:32.770 --> 00:54:37.750
So, yeah, I will like yell, save bandit for you, for your kid's birthday.
所以，对，我会愿意为你、为你孩子的生日大喊“救救班迪”。

1407
00:54:38.330 --> 00:54:38.610
Sure.
当然。

1408
00:54:38.790 --> 00:54:39.370
Why not?
为什么不呢？

1409
00:54:39.730 --> 00:54:39.930
Yeah.
对。

1410
00:54:40.150 --> 00:54:41.470
I'm super proud of it.
我对此超级骄傲。

1411
00:54:41.570 --> 00:54:41.730
Yeah.
对。

1412
00:54:41.750 --> 00:54:43.970
You know, like, why would I get over it?
你知道的，就像，我为什么要放下这个？

1413
00:54:44.110 --> 00:54:45.690
You know, when people say that.
你知道的，当人们那么说的时候。

1414
00:54:45.810 --> 00:54:48.150
Kate does the, she does the best cameos.
凯特做的，她做的客串是最棒的。

1415
00:54:48.330 --> 00:54:49.230
She really does.
真的是这样。

1416
00:54:49.430 --> 00:54:49.510
Yeah.
对。

1417
00:54:49.610 --> 00:54:51.230
And she did one for my daughter.
她还为我女儿拍了一个。

1418
00:54:51.390 --> 00:54:52.330
She actually knew it was from me.
她其实知道那是送给我的。

1419
00:54:52.450 --> 00:54:56.550
We had met once, but the fact that she will say all the stuff and then go to her piano,
我们曾见过一次，但她居然会说完全部那些话，然后走向她的钢琴，

1420
00:54:56.710 --> 00:54:57.350
play the theme song.
弹奏主题曲。

1421
00:54:57.430 --> 00:54:59.050
I'm like, oh, it's so amazing.
我就觉得，哦，这太棒了。

1422
00:54:59.230 --> 00:54:59.570
I know.
我懂。

1423
00:54:59.730 --> 00:55:01.230
It's exactly what a fan wants.
这正是粉丝想要的东西。

1424
00:55:01.370 --> 00:55:03.250
And I like to give that to people.
而我也喜欢把这带给别人。

1425
00:55:03.470 --> 00:55:05.470
I mean, I didn't grow up in Hollywood.
我是说，我不是在好莱坞长大的。

1426
00:55:05.490 --> 00:55:07.170
I didn't grow up in this world.
我不是在这个圈子里长大的。

1427
00:55:07.350 --> 00:55:12.130
I grew up in St. Louis, Missouri, going to skate parks and, you know, being in theater club.
我在密苏里州圣路易斯长大，去滑板公园，你知道的，参加戏剧社。

1428
00:55:12.130 --> 00:55:18.390
And, oh my gosh, to have, like, someone from that world that I dreamed about, like, say
而且，天哪，如果能让那个我梦想中的世界里的人，比如，说出

1429
00:55:18.390 --> 00:55:22.890
my name or shake my hand or take a picture with me, just how meaningful that would be.
我的名字，或者跟我握手，或者跟我合影，那该是多么有意义啊。

1430
00:55:23.150 --> 00:55:23.330
That's so cool.
那太酷了。

1431
00:55:23.430 --> 00:55:25.130
So I love to, like, give that out.
所以我喜欢，把这种体验送出去。

1432
00:55:25.310 --> 00:55:25.710
Yeah.
对。

1433
00:55:25.710 --> 00:55:26.410
Anytime I can.
只要有机会。

1434
00:55:26.830 --> 00:55:27.570
That's so amazing.
这太惊艳了。

1435
00:55:27.790 --> 00:55:27.870
Yeah.
对。

1436
00:55:28.390 --> 00:55:31.950
That's how I feel like if people come to my Instagram, I'm like, price of admission,
这就是我的感受，如果人们来到我的Instagram，我就会说，这就是门票价格，

1437
00:55:32.090 --> 00:55:32.270
buddy.
老兄。

1438
00:55:32.770 --> 00:55:34.270
You're going to get a lot of the office.
你会看到大量关于《办公室》的内容。

1439
00:55:34.970 --> 00:55:36.170
How else did you find me?
不然你怎么会找到我？

1440
00:55:36.390 --> 00:55:37.150
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

1441
00:55:37.610 --> 00:55:39.450
Oh, is it because I love hummingbirds?
哦，是因为我喜欢蜂鸟吗？

1442
00:55:39.570 --> 00:55:40.350
Is that why you're here?
这就是你来这里的理由吗？

1443
00:55:40.490 --> 00:55:42.430
Did you call 1-800-DENIS at some point?
你曾经打过 1-800-DENIS 的电话吗？

1444
00:55:42.710 --> 00:55:43.150
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

1445
00:55:43.550 --> 00:55:50.170
I will say that one of my most viral Instagram posts was, I brought it back from when I got
我要说，我最火的 Instagram 帖子之一，是我把它从我得以

1446
00:55:50.170 --> 00:55:50.850
to visit the set.
参观片场的那次搬了回来。

1447
00:55:50.850 --> 00:55:55.110
But I sat at the reception desk and put the phone to my ear.
但我坐在前台，把手机贴在耳边。

1448
00:55:55.270 --> 00:55:58.150
So a few years ago, I put just birdhouse skateboards.
所以几年前，我只发了鸟屋滑板。

1449
00:55:58.250 --> 00:55:58.630
This is Tony.
我是托尼。

1450
00:55:58.910 --> 00:55:59.810
Oh, that's so cool.
哦，那太酷了。

1451
00:55:59.810 --> 00:56:00.890
I was going to ask.
我正想问呢。

1452
00:56:01.050 --> 00:56:01.770
Yes, that's amazing.
对，太惊人了。

1453
00:56:01.770 --> 00:56:02.170
That went huge.
那可太火了。

1454
00:56:02.690 --> 00:56:03.530
Oh, that's great.
哦，那太棒了。

1455
00:56:03.530 --> 00:56:04.330
People are like, how the hell?
人们都在想，到底是怎么回事？

1456
00:56:04.590 --> 00:56:05.010
What?
什么？

1457
00:56:05.210 --> 00:56:05.850
Where did you?
你是在哪儿……？

1458
00:56:05.990 --> 00:56:07.590
It was just like, because it's a time warp.
就感觉，因为这就像是个时光倒流的地方。

1459
00:56:07.970 --> 00:56:08.170
Yeah.
是啊。

1460
00:56:08.550 --> 00:56:08.870
Yeah.
对。

1461
00:56:09.130 --> 00:56:10.190
It totally is.
确实如此。

1462
00:56:10.710 --> 00:56:12.150
Does the fame ever bother you?
名气有困扰过你吗？

1463
00:56:12.730 --> 00:56:16.210
No, I, only if it interferes with my family time.
没有，我……只有在它干扰到我和家人相处的时候。

1464
00:56:16.610 --> 00:56:21.190
If I get stopped and it gets tricky and, you know, if I'm traveling with my kids or whatnot
如果我被拦下来情况变得有点棘手，你知道的，如果我和孩子们一起旅行或者别的什么

1465
00:56:21.190 --> 00:56:23.910
and I feel like they're getting slided.
然后我觉得他们被冷落了。

1466
00:56:24.210 --> 00:56:24.930
Uncomfortable or something.
或者感到不自在什么的。

1467
00:56:25.130 --> 00:56:25.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1468
00:56:25.510 --> 00:56:25.810
Yeah.
对。

1469
00:56:25.950 --> 00:56:28.230
Or if I feel like it's just taking away from that.
或者我觉得它占用了陪伴的时间。

1470
00:56:28.430 --> 00:56:29.890
But that's rare, honestly.
不过说实话，这种情况很少见。

1471
00:56:30.050 --> 00:56:33.830
And I mean, I still get to ride my skateboard for a living.
而且我是说，我依然能靠滑滑板谋生。

1472
00:56:34.470 --> 00:56:36.710
I get paid to talk about skateboarding.
我靠谈论滑板赚钱。

1473
00:56:36.950 --> 00:56:39.210
Like, it's just such a dream come true.
就像是，梦想成真了一样。

1474
00:56:39.290 --> 00:56:41.270
And I can't believe I still get to do it.
而且我真不敢相信我到现在还能做这个。

1475
00:56:41.370 --> 00:56:42.550
So I'm super thankful.
所以我超级感激。

1476
00:56:42.550 --> 00:56:46.370
And, you know, I'm not some, I don't think I'm some polarizing figure.
而且，你知道的，我不是那种……我不觉得自己是个备受争议的人物。

1477
00:56:46.570 --> 00:56:51.790
So people are generally very nice and happy when I, when they see me.
所以人们通常都非常友善，看到我时都很高兴。

1478
00:56:53.190 --> 00:56:55.710
And our video game series was a huge hit.
我们的电子游戏系列大获成功。

1479
00:56:55.830 --> 00:56:56.850
So they like to talk about that.
所以他们喜欢聊这个。

1480
00:56:56.930 --> 00:56:58.310
And I played it.
而且我也玩过。

1481
00:56:58.430 --> 00:56:59.510
So I speak their language.
所以我懂他们的语言。

1482
00:56:59.830 --> 00:57:00.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1483
00:57:00.450 --> 00:57:00.650
Yeah.
对。

1484
00:57:01.090 --> 00:57:02.610
Are you good at your own video game?
你玩自己的游戏玩得好吗？

1485
00:57:02.870 --> 00:57:03.170
Yes.
对。

1486
00:57:03.310 --> 00:57:04.610
I'm good at playing with myself.
我自己跟自己玩挺厉害的。

1487
00:57:05.970 --> 00:57:08.110
That was a very Michael Scott thing to say.
这话很有迈克·斯科特的风格。

1488
00:57:08.130 --> 00:57:08.510
That's what she said.
她以前可不是这么说的。

1489
00:57:08.550 --> 00:57:09.410
It really was.
确实很像。

1490
00:57:09.930 --> 00:57:11.570
Well, should we do our call sheet questions?
好吧，我们要不要开始问通告单上的问题？

1491
00:57:11.570 --> 00:57:12.610
Let's do it.
开始吧。

1492
00:57:12.690 --> 00:57:13.250
Let's do it.
来吧。

1493
00:57:13.390 --> 00:57:13.630
Okay.
好的。

1494
00:57:14.250 --> 00:57:15.250
Here they are.
问题来了。

1495
00:57:15.390 --> 00:57:15.890
Number one.
第一题。

1496
00:57:16.590 --> 00:57:19.390
What was your very first entertainment job?
你的第一份娱乐行业的工作是什么？

1497
00:57:20.890 --> 00:57:24.070
I got to, I was on Captain Kangaroo.
我曾上过《袋鼠船长》。

1498
00:57:24.910 --> 00:57:25.690
You were?
真的吗？

1499
00:57:25.870 --> 00:57:26.630
How old were you?
你当时多大？

1500
00:57:26.850 --> 00:57:27.650
I was skateboarding.
我当时在玩滑板。

1501
00:57:27.790 --> 00:57:29.010
I was like 11.
我当时大概 11 岁。

1502
00:57:29.510 --> 00:57:30.090
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

1503
00:57:30.110 --> 00:57:30.330
Maybe 12.
也许 12 岁吧。

1504
00:57:30.950 --> 00:57:32.670
Did all the ping pong balls drop?
所有乒乓球都落地了吗？

1505
00:57:32.750 --> 00:57:32.950
No.
没有。

1506
00:57:33.230 --> 00:57:36.270
They shot the, I didn't understand how TV worked at the time.
他们拍了……我当时不懂电视是怎么运作的。

1507
00:57:36.370 --> 00:57:39.330
So I thought Captain Kangaroo was coming to the skate park and we're going to do this whole
所以我以为袋鼠船长要来滑板公园，然后我们要搞一场

1508
00:57:39.330 --> 00:57:39.570
thing.
大动作。

1509
00:57:39.570 --> 00:57:43.950
And this crew came, shot me skating and they made a little segment about it.
结果来了一支摄制组，拍了我滑滑板，还做了一段关于这的短片。

1510
00:57:44.450 --> 00:57:44.910
Oh.
哦。

1511
00:57:45.570 --> 00:57:46.030
Okay.
好吧。

1512
00:57:46.030 --> 00:57:47.730
So you didn't go to the set, but still.
所以你没去片场，但也算啦。

1513
00:57:47.950 --> 00:57:52.510
I didn't get to go to the set, but I mean, we sat and watched Captain Kangaroo one morning
我没能去片场，但我的意思是，我们有一天早上坐在一起看袋鼠船长

1514
00:57:52.510 --> 00:57:53.170
and I was on it.
然后我就在上面了。

1515
00:57:53.270 --> 00:57:54.150
That's wild.
太疯狂了。

1516
00:57:54.270 --> 00:57:54.410
Yeah.
是啊。

1517
00:57:54.630 --> 00:57:55.390
That's pretty cool.
这挺酷的。

1518
00:57:56.030 --> 00:57:56.790
Number two.
第二个问题。

1519
00:57:57.330 --> 00:58:01.170
Do you speak any other languages or play a musical instrument?
你会说其他语言还是会演奏乐器？

1520
00:58:01.170 --> 00:58:03.550
I speak a little bit of French.
我会说一点法语。

1521
00:58:04.290 --> 00:58:09.790
I took a couple of years and then I spent about six weeks right after high school in France.
我学了几年，高中毕业后又在法国呆了大约六周。

1522
00:58:10.770 --> 00:58:13.070
So I understand it more than I speak it.
所以我听懂的比说得要多。

1523
00:58:13.330 --> 00:58:15.310
Like we were there for the Olympics over the summer.
比如夏天我们在那里看奥运会。

1524
00:58:15.470 --> 00:58:22.510
I managed to navigate our family through some tricky security checkpoints thanks to my French.
多亏了我的法语，我成功带家人通过了一些棘手的安检关卡。

1525
00:58:22.510 --> 00:58:26.710
So I feel like that was worth all the two years of it in school.
所以我感觉这没白费我在学校学的那两年。

1526
00:58:26.970 --> 00:58:28.190
And I used to play violin.
我以前还会拉小提琴。

1527
00:58:28.570 --> 00:58:29.730
Do you still play violin?
你现在还拉小提琴吗？

1528
00:58:29.890 --> 00:58:30.010
No.
不拉了。

1529
00:58:30.270 --> 00:58:40.650
My music teacher, when I was 12, he wanted me to do these extracurricular school concerts and stuff
我 12 岁时，我的音乐老师希望我参加这些课外学校音乐会之类的活动

1530
00:58:40.650 --> 00:58:41.610
on weekends.
在周末。

1531
00:58:41.610 --> 00:58:43.350
And that was when I would have to go compete.
而那正好是我要去比赛的时候。

1532
00:58:43.690 --> 00:58:47.070
And I told him, no, I have to, I'm going to compete in the skateboard event.
我告诉他不行，我得去，我要去参加滑板比赛。

1533
00:58:47.110 --> 00:58:48.510
And he said, well, you can't do both.
他说，那两样你不能兼得。

1534
00:58:49.150 --> 00:58:49.430
What?
什么？

1535
00:58:50.270 --> 00:58:52.310
You had to pick violin or skateboarding.
你必须在小提琴和滑板之间二选一。

1536
00:58:52.470 --> 00:58:53.170
According to him.
按他的说法是这样。

1537
00:58:53.770 --> 00:58:55.470
That was a real sliding doors moment.
那真是一个命运转折的瞬间。

1538
00:58:55.550 --> 00:58:56.270
It was for sure.
确实是的。

1539
00:58:56.290 --> 00:58:59.670
And I said, okay, well, I, this is way more fun for me.
我说，好吧，我觉得这个对我有意思得多。

1540
00:58:59.790 --> 00:59:01.730
And I didn't think I was choosing a future anyway.
而且我当时也没想过是在选择未来。

1541
00:59:01.890 --> 00:59:02.150
I was 12.
我才 12 岁。

1542
00:59:02.290 --> 00:59:02.750
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吧？

1543
00:59:02.750 --> 00:59:03.250
I know, exactly.
我懂，确实。

1544
00:59:03.530 --> 00:59:06.890
I'm not going to be a concert violinist or I'm not going to be a pro skateboard.
我又不会成为音乐会小提琴家，也不会成为职业滑板手。

1545
00:59:07.010 --> 00:59:08.590
I'm just, I just love doing this.
我只是，我就是喜欢做这个。

1546
00:59:08.670 --> 00:59:11.330
And so, and so I chose, and I wish that I hadn't quit.
所以，所以我就做了选择，但我也希望当时没有放弃。

1547
00:59:11.330 --> 00:59:15.890
I wish I hadn't really listened to him like that, but he was the music teacher and he wasn't
我希望当时没有那样听他的话，但他毕竟是音乐老师，而且他

1548
00:59:15.890 --> 00:59:18.190
going to let me keep being in his class.
不让我继续留在他的班里。

1549
00:59:18.330 --> 00:59:19.110
Yeah, that's not.
对，那可真不。

1550
00:59:19.130 --> 00:59:20.190
Because I wasn't doing the other stuff.
因为我没有做那些别的事。

1551
00:59:20.350 --> 00:59:23.010
I tried to pick it up again and it wasn't like riding a bike.
我试图重新捡起它，但这可不是一学就会、永生难忘的。

1552
00:59:23.550 --> 00:59:24.430
It was too.
才怪呢。

1553
00:59:24.610 --> 00:59:25.430
That's interesting.
真有意思。

1554
00:59:25.970 --> 00:59:26.330
All right.
行吧。

1555
00:59:26.950 --> 00:59:29.610
What's a place you've been to that you absolutely loved?
你曾经去过哪个地方，是你绝对深爱的？

1556
00:59:30.250 --> 00:59:30.990
Firstly, Japan.
首先，日本。

1557
00:59:31.530 --> 00:59:38.590
I got to go there when I was 14 for a TV show called basically Wonder Kids or Amazing Kids.
我14岁时去过那里，为了一个基本上叫作“奇迹小子”或“神奇儿童”的电视节目。

1558
00:59:39.350 --> 00:59:41.170
And in my later years, Iceland.
后来大一点的时候，是冰岛。

1559
00:59:41.890 --> 00:59:44.190
Oh, I'm going to Iceland this summer.
噢，我今年夏天要去冰岛。

1560
00:59:44.310 --> 00:59:44.750
Iceland's so cool.
冰岛太酷了。

1561
00:59:44.950 --> 00:59:45.650
Oh, I can't wait.
噢，我迫不及待了。

1562
00:59:45.870 --> 00:59:45.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1563
00:59:46.590 --> 00:59:47.170
All right.
好啦。

1564
00:59:47.330 --> 00:59:47.830
Next one.
下一个。

1565
00:59:48.050 --> 00:59:49.230
What do you like to do on the weekends?
你周末喜欢做些什么？

1566
00:59:49.790 --> 00:59:56.850
I like to try to be home and have our kids come home because they are all pretty much
我喜欢尽量待在家裡，让孩子们也回家，因为他们基本上都已经

1567
00:59:56.850 --> 00:59:57.110
gone.
搬出去了。

1568
00:59:57.290 --> 00:59:58.430
We only have one at home now.
我们现在只有一个孩子还住在家里。

1569
00:59:58.430 --> 01:00:06.930
My daughter, we have five boys and they all are quote adults, but they do tend to migrate
我的女儿，我们有五个男孩，他们都算是成年人了，但他们往往会在

1570
01:00:06.930 --> 01:00:08.010
back home on the weekends.
周末聚回家里。

1571
01:00:08.470 --> 01:00:09.190
Oh, that's nice.
噢，那真好。

1572
01:00:09.190 --> 01:00:11.690
I like to try to be home in case that happens.
我喜欢尽量待在家裡，以防这种事情发生。

1573
01:00:12.550 --> 01:00:13.630
I love that.
我太喜欢这样了。

1574
01:00:13.950 --> 01:00:14.150
All right.
好啦。

1575
01:00:14.270 --> 01:00:14.810
Last one.
最后一个。

1576
01:00:15.130 --> 01:00:16.330
Favorite midnight snack.
最喜欢的午夜小吃。

1577
01:00:17.290 --> 01:00:17.690
Hmm.
嗯……

1578
01:00:18.370 --> 01:00:19.330
That's tricky.
这挺难选的。

1579
01:00:20.090 --> 01:00:20.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1580
01:00:20.530 --> 01:00:21.010
I don't like it.
我不喜欢这样。

1581
01:00:22.770 --> 01:00:24.550
I like this kind of sweet popcorn.
我喜欢这种甜爆米花。

1582
01:00:25.170 --> 01:00:26.010
Sweet popcorn?
甜爆米花？

1583
01:00:26.350 --> 01:00:26.470
Yeah.
对。

1584
01:00:26.470 --> 01:00:28.050
Like a kettle corn kind of thing?
就像大锅爆米花那种的？

1585
01:00:28.190 --> 01:00:28.490
Yeah.
对。

1586
01:00:28.730 --> 01:00:29.790
But not too sweet.
但不要太甜。

1587
01:00:29.950 --> 01:00:31.950
You know, the boom chicka boom.
你知道的，就那种Boom Chicka Boom。

1588
01:00:31.950 --> 01:00:32.630
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

1589
01:00:33.050 --> 01:00:34.070
That one's pretty good.
那个挺好吃的。

1590
01:00:34.070 --> 01:00:39.930
Either that or I go crackers, happy cow cheese, and salami.
要么就是苏打饼干配乐芝牛乳酪和萨拉米香肠。

1591
01:00:40.410 --> 01:00:42.150
You're speaking Antelope's language.
你完全说到安蒂洛普的心坎里去了。

1592
01:00:42.330 --> 01:00:43.110
That's all I ever want.
那正是我一直想要的。

1593
01:00:43.110 --> 01:00:44.230
It's near and dear to her heart.
这可是她的最爱啊。

1594
01:00:44.230 --> 01:00:45.070
That's a good one.
这个不错。

1595
01:00:45.110 --> 01:00:46.270
That's my favorite snack.
那是我的最爱零食。

1596
01:00:46.490 --> 01:00:50.870
A tangent to that question is, if you were standing in line for pretzel day, what's your
顺着这个问题延伸一下，如果你正在排队买椒盐卷饼日，你会

1597
01:00:50.870 --> 01:00:51.130
order?
点什么？

1598
01:00:51.630 --> 01:00:52.390
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

1599
01:00:52.910 --> 01:00:58.350
It would either be cinnamon and sugar or frosted, but I don't care about the sprinkles and I
要么是肉桂糖味的，要么是糖霜味的，但我不在乎那些糖屑，也不在乎

1600
01:00:58.350 --> 01:01:00.010
don't care about all the other accoutrements.
其他乱七八糟的配料。

1601
01:01:00.510 --> 01:01:00.770
Okay.
好的。

1602
01:01:01.050 --> 01:01:02.070
I'm cinnamon sugar.
我是肉桂糖味。

1603
01:01:02.230 --> 01:01:02.970
I'm cinnamon sugar.
我是肉桂糖味。

1604
01:01:03.270 --> 01:01:03.650
Yeah.
对。

1605
01:01:04.070 --> 01:01:04.370
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1606
01:01:04.990 --> 01:01:06.570
Yeah, like a cinnamon toast vibe.
对，有点像肉桂吐司的感觉。

1607
01:01:06.750 --> 01:01:06.970
Yes.
是的。

1608
01:01:07.010 --> 01:01:07.210
Yep.
没错。

1609
01:01:07.350 --> 01:01:07.670
Yes.
是的。

1610
01:01:07.970 --> 01:01:08.530
That is it.
就是这样。

1611
01:01:08.750 --> 01:01:09.430
It's pretty great.
这真是太棒了。

1612
01:01:10.230 --> 01:01:12.370
So am I going to walk out the door and there's going to be a pretzel cart?
那我走出门外就会看到一个卖软饼干的手推车吗？

1613
01:01:13.110 --> 01:01:14.810
No, I wish we planned ahead.
